{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': '1608299627', 'answerTime': 'Jul 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374303600, 'question': 'You bought level one . Will you buy the next levels?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Midway through I tried out Pimsleur and I found it a lot more practical than Rosetta Stone. Eventually I switched to group classes. In general I would say RS is great for a quick start and vocabulary, Pimsleur is great for practical phrases but in the end there's nothing like a real teacher."}
