{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': '1617168718', 'answerTime': 'Jan 20, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421740800, 'question': "My little kid want to use this sw but she can't read English but Korean. Can I select Korean as guide language for Mandarin when I install the sw ?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The two languages are totally unrelated. Korean is more related to Japanese then Chinese. Korean has borrowed some Chinese words but the grammars and word order of the two languages are totally different. Like Japanese, Korean has an extensive system of verb suffixes and post positions unlike anything in Chinese. Occasionally Chinese characters are seen in Korea but they seemed to be more decorative in nature.'}
