{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00005A9VI', 'answerTime': 'Jul 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375081200, 'question': 'I use Quicken and TurboTax. Does MoneyDance work with TurboTax?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Turbotax won't import Moneydance data. Moneydance will export QIF and tab delimited but those won't go into Turbotax. I also use Turbotax. I just enter in the data manually. Years ago, I used quicken and did the import thing. I then had to double check and fix up. I think the manual method is actually faster and more reliable at the end of the day. Every year, I tell myself I'm going to try one of the other tax programs but then time runs short and I fall back on Turbotax. Maybe this year."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00005A9VI', 'answerTime': 'Jan 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420185600, 'question': 'Why does it take at least one whole minute to move from line to line, and in general so so slow as to be unusable?', 'answer': "I don't have that problem. Mine is quick. Ask on the help line."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00005A9VI', 'answerTime': 'Nov 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416211200, 'question': 'How do you print partial pages of pre-printed 3 check forms?', 'answer': 'No idea, I gave up on this program years ago.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00005A9VI', 'answerTime': 'Sep 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410159600, 'question': 'Why are there no instructions on how the system works? There are no books either (that I can find). Everything seems to require an assist by phone.', 'answer': 'You can print the entire manual.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00005A9VI', 'answerTime': 'Jul 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406703600, 'question': 'Does it come on a disc or download only', 'answer': "I believe it is download only, and I did a quick check on,the internet which confirms that. However, you get a registration number, which would allow you to re-download, if needed. Also, I have found Infinite Kind support to be extremely helpful and responsive. I sent several emails early on, and each was responded to. Good luck. It's not Quicken, but I really love it."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00005A9VI', 'answerTime': 'Feb 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393315200, 'question': 'can I import msm money onto moneydance', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Not directly. The way I got my data into Moneydance was to import it into Quicken and then export it as a QIF file. If Microsoft Money supports QIF output you could export directly. Although I really like Moneydance, I'd gladly go back to Microsoft Money if I had the opportunity. Money was an absolutely perfect fit for my needs while Moneydance is just very well designed for my needs."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00005A9VI', 'answerTime': 'Feb 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393315200, 'question': 'Will it work for property management?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'That depends on what you are trying to get the software to do. If you are asking whether it can handle basic asset reporting and accounting, the answer is yes. If you are trying to get it to print invoices or do credit checks or any other specialized property management functions; sorry, the answer is no.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00005A9VI', 'answerTime': 'Jan 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388908800, 'question': 'does money allow using envelopes for monthly income and expense', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Not exactly in the sense you mean. It has a fairly extensive budgeting function but I've never used it so I can't vouch for it. All I can say from experience is that the program has worked very well for my needs except for a couple of minor nagging issues that I really should contact the vendor about as there is probably a solution already out there."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00005A9VI', 'answerTime': 'Jun 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371711600, 'question': 'does is work with chase bank', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I had another major bank, but I would guess chase uses compatible system. Sorry no help, but MD faqs should help.'}
