{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00005MOTG', 'answerTime': 'Jan 16, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421395200, 'question': 'can i install this on a desktop. even tho it has no operating system installed', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'No. An "upgrade" version requires a previous version to be existing (or at least have the installation disk(s) for the previous version). That said, XP is no longer supported and is vunerable to security attacks. MS is providing no further updates (as of April 2014). But if ou must have XP, then look for the "Full" version.'}
