{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000063EMX', 'answerTime': 'Apr 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397631600, 'question': "I lost everything in a fire. Someone got me version 5 limited edition. Do you know if I can jump (upgrade) from that to 7? (I'm on a used XP)", 'answer': 'Yes, you can. Simply put, yes. I used to have an XP. It does work on it. 7 is old, It will even work on windows 2000. Which I also, had where it worked. So yes, go right ahead and upgrade to 7.'}
{'answer': "Hi! It means there is a more recent edition available, but this one is still fully functional. This one is the 7.0 upgrade which was first available in 2002. The platforms it called for when originally produced were Windows NT / 98 / 2000 / Me / XP / 95. I believe it's the last one they made before it became the CD versions. I don't know a lot more about it than that unfortunately. The copy I am offering is brand new - still shrinkwrapped. I hope this answers your questions.", 'asin': 'B000063EMX', 'answerTime': '4 days ago', 'question': 'What do you mean by [ Old Version ] ?', 'questionType': 'open-ended'}
