{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00022PTI4', 'answerTime': 'Nov 28, 2009', 'unixTime': 1259395200, 'question': 'windows xp pro - used: How is it possible to buy a "used" copy of xp and have it work if it can only be installed on one computer?', 'answer': "I bought a new PC recently - my old motherboard finally gave up and died. I installed my copy of XP on it and it activated with no problemo. I do not think that it really prevents you from installing on other PCs but I do not know if the limit to installs is based on timeframe e.g. twice a year, or your computer hardware ids. XP can't be too restrictive otherwise ppl would not be able to upgrade hardware and their customer base would be more 'annoyed' than usual. Check out this link - NellyE says the limit is once every 4 months http://uk.answers.yahoo.com/question/index?qid=20090910100643AAVFf6q"}
