{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00022PTRU', 'answerTime': 'May 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398927600, 'question': 'I currently have a laptop with Windows 8. I hate it! Can I install Windows XP with SP2 over this system?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Don\'t try having both OSs at once. My suggestion is to decant all your apps and files to an external "save drive, and install XP. If it looks like the Windows 8 is still there, you didn\'t do it right and you (or somebody who know how to "kill" Windows 8) will have to do it again. That said, yes. XP with SP2 is a going proposition. Microsoft is many patches "ahead" of plain-vanilla SP2, so caution...'}
