{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002DOECA', 'answerTime': 'Sep 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380351600, 'question': 'will Digital Image Pro 9 work with windows 7?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't know if Digital Image Pro 9 will work with win7. I have digital Image suite 10, and it was not designed for win7, but I installed it anyway and it works. There are a few features that do not work exactly right, but the things I use the most do work ok. It is a really intuitive program and is so easy to use that I use it instead of the newer photo processing programs that I have."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002G71T0', 'answerTime': 'Aug 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376809200, 'question': "I have an iMac 4.2 / PowerPC g4 2.1. Will this allow me to reboot the computer to a fresh install? I don't have the discs that came originally.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Since this is a retail disc, then yes, I believe this version should work. For best results, you may be able to find iMac G4 discs on eBay--but, again, these should work fine. And, finally, as an extra tip, if you can, see if you can try Leopard instead. It\'s more modern and better supported by older apps. And, since you\'re a 4,2 and not a 6,1 model, you may need to either install 10.5 through FireWire or over clock your G4 speed. On this last part, you\'ll have to check if your "official" (meaning it should install flawlessly) maximum OS stops at 10.4.11 or not. Hope this helps! Good luck! :-)'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002G71T0', 'answerTime': 'Dec 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386144000, 'question': 'Is this PPC, Intel or Universal?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "PPC only. 10.6 (Snow Leopard) was the first only Intel and 10.5 (Leopard) ran on both Intel and PPC. Some Macs shipped with Tiger, but had slightly different disks that won't work on other models. Hope this helps."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002G71T0', 'answerTime': 'Mar 23, 2008', 'unixTime': 1206255600, 'question': 'How many Versions of Tiger are there? Where do I get that????', 'answer': 'Make sure you\'re online and click the Apple menu (upper-left of screen the screen in the menu bar) and click "Software Update...". Then it will check for updates and you can click "Install". It will update you to version 10.4.11 for free.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002G71T0', 'answerTime': 'Apr 5, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428217200, 'question': 'Will it work on my PowerMac G4 533MHz Digital Audio build 8A428 OS X 10.4 PPC', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It works on my G4 867 MGzPowerbook. I misplaced my disc and had to buy a new one when I replaced the hard drive. I then upgraded it to 10.4.11 on the apple website. From your description you already have 'tiger' installed on the computer."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002G71T0', 'answerTime': 'Feb 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422864000, 'question': 'Is this designed for Powermac G4', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'My machine is an eMac G4 with a PowerPC processor, and it worked for me. I believe it will work for your machine as well if it has the same specs. 10.4.11 is as far as you can go, though.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002G71T0', 'answerTime': 'Nov 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415606400, 'question': 'I want to factory reset my Ibook g4 does this work?', 'answer': 'It worked perfectly for me to reload my book.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002G71T0', 'answerTime': 'Oct 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412838000, 'question': 'I have an 2005-06 iMac OS X 10.4 I can no longer find my original restore disc, will this work?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I did a clean install with this and worked fine'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002G71T0', 'answerTime': 'Jun 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401951600, 'question': 'Are these Cds or dvds because my emac only has a cd drive?', 'answer': 'First, they are CDs and secondly, your iMac DOES have a DVD/CD drive. Unless, of course, it predates DVDs and then OS X 10 probably will not run on your device either.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002G71T0', 'answerTime': 'Dec 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386316800, 'question': 'Will this work on an old Imac running OS 9?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'IT DEPENDS UPON YOU PROCESSOR. THE INFORMATION BELOW COMES DIRECTLY FROM THE APPLE WEB SITE. I HOPE IT HELPS YOU. To use Mac OS X v10.4, your Macintosh needs: A PowerPC G3, G4, or G5 processor Built-in FireWire At least 256 MB of RAM DVD drive (DVD-ROM), Combo (CD-RW/DVD-ROM) or SuperDrive (DVD-R) for installation At least 3 GB of free disk space; 4 GB if you install the XCode 2 Developer Tools Additional Information Notes Please be sure to read the "Before You Install" document included on the Mac OS X 10.4 installation disc for more important information. Mac OS X does not support processor upgrade cards. The amount of disk space required depends on your computer and how you choose to install Mac OS X. Not all PowerPC G3 processor-based Macs have built-in FireWire. BOB ANDERSON PETOSKEY, MI'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002G71T0', 'answerTime': 'Dec 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386230400, 'question': 'I wipe out my Mac HD IBook G4 1.2 GHz, and have no original installation disk. Will this copy of Apple Mac OS x will help me to get it back again?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, as long as you have the hard drive space, and enough RAM: "To use Mac OS X v10.4, your Macintosh needs: A PowerPC G3, G4, or G5 processor Built-in FireWire At least 256 MB of RAM DVD drive (DVD-ROM), Combo (CD-RW/DVD-ROM) or SuperDrive (DVD-R) for installation At least 3 GB of free disk space."'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002J6HV0', 'answerTime': 'Apr 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397286000, 'question': 'Will this work on Windows 7?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes. We use it on Windows 7. My kids like it and it teaches them basic math concepts. Recently I wanted my son to memorize basic math facts: addition/subtraction, multiplication, division. We did the trial at www (dot) reflexmath (dot) com. He's done 14 sessions of add/subtract and has gone from 11% to 50% fluency. He does it until the green light comes on 5 days a week."}
