{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000BR0NPO', 'answerTime': 'Jun 14, 2007', 'unixTime': 1181804400, 'question': 'How many licenses? How many licenses does the family pack include?', 'answer': 'From the Apple site (about Tiger, but I assume it will hold true for Leopard): "Family Pack Software License Agreement allows you to install and use one copy of the Apple Software on up to a maximum of five (5) Apple-labeled computers at a time as long as those computers are located in the same household and used by persons who occupy that same household. By "household" we mean a person or persons who share the same housing unit such as a home, apartment, mobile home or condominium, but shall also extend to student members who are primary residents of that household but residing at a separate on-campus location. This license does not extend to business or commercial users."'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000BR0NPO', 'answerTime': 'Oct 22, 2007', 'unixTime': 1193036400, 'question': '5 Licenses, but how many discs? I know the family pack can be used on up to 5 computers, but how many discs come in the package?', 'answer': 'Family pack has one disc and five serials. this is a good deal on amazon, $10 cheaper than apple'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000BR0NPO', 'answerTime': 'Apr 16, 2015', 'unixTime': 1429167600, 'question': 'Can I clean install this after formatting my hard drive? Or do I need to re-install 10.5.0 then upgrade with this one?', 'answer': 'Yes, you can clean install'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000BR0NPO', 'answerTime': 'Nov 4, 2007', 'unixTime': 1194159600, 'question': 'Leopard: older computers: Will Leopard run on those, or are they too old?', 'answer': 'If your systems match or super exceed the system requirements stated below, then both of your mac machines will more than likely run the new Leopard Operating System. I hope this post helps MAC OS X Leopard System Requirements: \x1a Processor must be any Intel, PowerPC G5 or G4 (at 867 MHz or faster) \x1a DVD drive (for installation of the operating system) \x1a Built-in FireWire \x1a At least 512 MB of RAM (additional RAM is recommended for development purposes) \x1a A built-in display or a display connected to an Apple-supplied video card \x1a At least 9 GB of disk space available'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000BR0NPO', 'answerTime': 'Jun 15, 2007', 'unixTime': 1181890800, 'question': 'Media - 1 out of 5 of my Macs has CD only. How do I install on this computer?', 'answer': 'Just hook the CD only Mac to your DVD reading Mac via Firewire and reboot the older Mac holding down T key. That mac will then appear on desktop of your newer mac and you can install from the DVD.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000BR0NPO', 'answerTime': 'Oct 17, 2007', 'unixTime': 1192604400, 'question': 'Shipping Leopard from Amazon? If I order from Amazon, when would I receive my Leopard?', 'answer': 'I would guess it would be similar to pre-ordering dvds, books, etc. In my experience, they tend to ship out the same day of the official release... so when you get it would depend on how you had it shipped (a day or so after). If you must have it immediately... pick up a copy at an apple store the morning of the 26th.'}
