{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000HCTYTE', 'answerTime': 'Jan 8, 2007', 'unixTime': 1168243200, 'question': 'Is Vista 32bit and 64bit on the same DVD or seperate versions? Hi Anyone know if this copy of Vista comes with both 32bit and 64bit versions or will we need to buy 32bit and 64bit versions separately?', 'answer': "It's true that both versions are supposed to be available on the same disc. Supposedly it should ask you on the first screen whether you want to install the 64bit or 32bit version after it checks to see if you have a 64bit processor. Otherwise it just gives the option for 32bit installation."}
