{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000HCVR12', 'answerTime': 'Apr 30, 2009', 'unixTime': 1241074800, 'question': 'Access 2007 info: How can I add the pictures to the table so they show up in the forms?', 'answer': 'Pictures would be considered an OLE object. Just set up a field in one of the tables containing membership information as an OLE object field. Keep in mind, however, that storing images INSIDE the database (embedding) versus just storing the link to them (linking) takes up HUGE amounts of space in the database. Only embed very small images, or images that you cannot link successfully from outside the program.'}
