{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000HKMQ64', 'answerTime': 'Dec 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386921600, 'question': 'I have a laptop using Win 8 And just recently inherited a Galaxy Tab2 10.1 any info on how I can load this onto my tab for reading on the go?', 'answer': "Being sensitive to the people around me, I find it best to covertly read my MAD Magazine cloaked in a US News & World Report, People, O Magazine, Car & Driver, or Playboy. MAD may be considered NSFW. However, if you want to read it stashed within a tablet, the DVD is basically a stack of .pdf files. So, you'd need a DVD reader to connect to something (maybe your laptop) and then just manually drag all the .pdf files somehow over to your tablet. If your tablet won't open .pdf files then you're going to be dead meat, unless some Cloud-based service (Adobe) will convert them for you. However, I'm not sure how well satirical American humor will go over in a Korean (or Chinese or Japanese) tablet. Different cultures you know."}
