{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000QO76HU', 'answerTime': 'Dec 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388044800, 'question': "Can YNAB create year-end tax reports, similar to Quicken? I don't import directly to Turbo Tax, but instead use Quickens summary reports.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Sort of. I make sure to set up categories for business income and deductible expenses and make sure to categorize those expenses when I enter them throughout the year. At the end of the year I just print out a category report and I have my numbers.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000QO76HU', 'answerTime': 'Apr 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1365231600, 'question': 'Can you print reports, etc?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, reports can be printed. The graphs and the transactions.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000QO76HU', 'answerTime': 'Jan 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1358582400, 'question': 'I use computer checks with Microsoft Money. Does YNAB have the capabilities to print checks?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "No and that's not a feature I see them offering anytime soon. YNAB is first and foremost a budgeting methodology and the software helps its users to budget accordingly. While it has several nice features, they are all focused on the core of the software's purpose: the budget."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000QO76HU', 'answerTime': 'Jun 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403766000, 'question': 'Does this work well for canada?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes! It only supports one currency per budget, but can do any currency. There are many international users on the support forums'}
