{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001CPHTAQ', 'answerTime': 'Feb 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391760000, 'question': 'Using Sony Vegas platinum, How do you un-split or rejoin events that have been previously split on the time line and undo is no longer an option', 'answer': 'If they were originally joined, as best I recall, there is a specific selection in one of the drop down menus to &lt;rejoin sections&gt;. Or you can just butt them together on the time line. If you have deleted the segment, you can put the whole video segment back up on another time line, find the section you want and split it off and put it in where you want to and delete the parts before and after.'}
