{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001EJTO8A', 'answerTime': 'Feb 20, 2009', 'unixTime': 1235116800, 'question': 'Fitting a video clip that is too long: How can I make it fit on one DVD?', 'answer': "Most software will automatically compress as needed. I use Sony Vegas Movie Studio and that's what it does, at least with avi files. When you are ready to burn, it will warn you that it needs to compress to fit on the target disk. As far as working with other formats, you would just have to find out what formats the software handles or convert it. Another option is DL (double-layer) disks."}
