{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002ABOYXG', 'answerTime': 'Aug 19, 2010', 'unixTime': 1282201200, 'question': 'photo editing: Pixelmator - does it do red eye reduction?', 'answer': "I don't have Pixelmator YET but am going to purchase it in the short term future. IPhoto does a great job of fixing red-eye. Just open your photo, select edit in the lower left of the screen & a red eye option comes up. You can either let IPhoto auto fix the red eye or you can manually fix it yourself. I think it works great!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002ASAEH4', 'answerTime': 'Sep 29, 2009', 'unixTime': 1254207600, 'question': 'Famly Tree Maker: Essentials vs Platinum versions: Anybody know the differences between the two versions?', 'answer': 'It looks like the Deluxe and Platinum versions come with a DVD that has digital copies of genealogy reference books while the Essentials version does not. The Deluxe has 10 books and the Platinum has 15. I am not sure if these are worth the upgrade or if they are available for free online anyway. Anyone know?'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002ASAEH4', 'answerTime': 'Mar 24, 2010', 'unixTime': 1269414000, 'question': 'New to Genealogy: Is this app considered user-friendly enough for someone who is just beginning to trace their ancestry and relatively ignorant in the field of genealogy?', 'answer': 'FTM 2010 is, in my opinion, the best out there and I have been working on genealogy since 2000. Use the help functions, the on-line tutorials and go take a class on this software at you local history or genalogy center. I strongly urge a beginner to go take a basic genealogy class to get you started.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002ASAEH4', 'answerTime': 'Nov 11, 2009', 'unixTime': 1257926400, 'question': 'Will FTM 2010 work in Windows7?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I asked that question myself, here\'s the answer I received "We appreciate your message. Family Tree Maker 2010 is compatible with and supported for use on both 32 and 64 bit versions of Windows 7. If there is anything else with which we might assist you, please let us know. Jen Member Solutions Ancestry.com http://ancestry.custhelp.com/"'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002ASAEH4', 'answerTime': 'Oct 23, 2010', 'unixTime': 1287817200, 'question': 'Importing data from an earlier version? Will this be able to import all my data from version 5 or will I have to re-enter it all?', 'answer': "I have FTM version 6. I am planning on buying FTM 2011. I believe you have to back up your family file to a floppy disk and then import all the information when you have your new FTM software installed. At least I hope things go this smoothly. I've noticed that FTM is no longer made by Broderbund but a different company. I hope this doesn't cause a problem."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002ASAEH4', 'answerTime': 'Mar 24, 2010', 'unixTime': 1269414000, 'question': 'Descendant Index/Report: Does anyone know if this is offered in the 2010 version?', 'answer': 'If I understand your question, yes, and I am sure it was in my 2008 version, too. FTM 2010 is far superior to 2008. I suggest upgrading to the Essentials version. If I understand what you mean, in 2010 you go to the Publish tab, select Relationship Reports, and then OUtline Descendant Report. Presto...you are done.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002ASAEH4', 'answerTime': 'May 7, 2011', 'unixTime': 1304751600, 'question': 'Why FTM and not just the online tree on Ancestory.com? What are the advantages of using FTM?', 'answer': 'The biggest advantage for me with Family Tree Maker is being able to print out reports (ancestor based, descendant charts etc. that include siblings) to hold in my hand and look over while searching files on ancestry.com. You can print reports and books from ancestry but they cost you big time, which may be fine when you are all finished but not until then.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002ASAEH4', 'answerTime': 'Jun 29, 2010', 'unixTime': 1277794800, 'question': 'Question on Ancestry.com access: I see that FTM includes 1 - 3 months of access, but I wonder, do they make you give them credit card info to get this free access, i.e. try to hook you in anyway?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I saw the following statement in someone else\'s review of FTM 10. Hope it helps. "Do note that when you sign up for your "free" month with this software, you will be required to enter billing information and they will start stealth charging you when the free month is up - so watch for that. "'}
