{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002DHLUWK', 'answerTime': 'Mar 4, 2012', 'unixTime': 1330848000, 'question': 'Buy now and FREE upgrade to Win8? If I were to buy this now will I get a free upgrade to Win 8?', 'answer': "Well, back in 2009 if you bought a Windows Vista PC starting from late June you could get a free Windows 7 upgrade, so probably in this case they will do the same from Windows 7 to 8 but in your case you won't qualify since you need to buy a new PC."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002DHLUWK', 'answerTime': 'Jan 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390982400, 'question': 'I wish to go from Windows Vista HomePremium 64-bit to Windows 7 HomePremium 64-bit. Is this the product I need?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, that is what I used to upgrade from Vista to Windows 7.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002DHLVII', 'answerTime': 'Sep 4, 2009', 'unixTime': 1252047600, 'question': '32 or 64 bit? Which version is it?', 'answer': "Each version of Windows 7 comes with BOTH the 32 and 64-bit discs. They're on seperate discs but your product key is interchangable (you cannot instal 1 machine with 32-bit and 1 with 64-bit however). I just got my copy of 7 Professional through the MSDNAA and I have to tell you: BEST OS from Microsoft yet!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002DHLVII', 'answerTime': 'Apr 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1364799600, 'question': 'Is this retail or oem? Does it have to stay on the first computer I load it on or will Microsoft let me move it to another computer in the future?', 'answer': 'Mine was retail. You will have to make sure that you do contact Microsoft if & when you want to move it to another computer. My license is for only "1" computer. I do have an OEM copy that has not been opened or used that is designed for system builders that I will sell for $150.00 & you pay shipping. Did I give you enough?'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002DHLVII', 'answerTime': 'Nov 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416556800, 'question': 'Why is the old version selling for more than three times that of the SP1 version?', 'answer': 'Hi, I believe you are referring to the OEM versions marked as SP1? OEM versions are not equivalent to retail versions as they do not come with transfer rights; you may not move your installation to a new computer. Also, most of the Win 7 items on this listing will be SP1 as both SP1 and non-SP1 Windows 7 retail are the same part number. Hope this helps!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002DHLVII', 'answerTime': 'Dec 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387267200, 'question': 'I\'ve had to have my HD wiped and am starting brand new. I want MS os7 Pro 64bit, but want to make sure I get the correct item with the "key". Seeing too many versions, ie. "Full", "branded", "OEM". What do I need to get? Your advise is appreciated.', 'answer': 'This is what you want. I used this dor my last gaming rig. It came with both 32 and 64 bit as well as the key.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002DHLVII', 'answerTime': 'Jan 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391068800, 'question': 'is there any other reason I would want a retail copy vs. OEM other than Microsoft support?', 'answer': "OEM versions of Windows 7 are identical to Retail versions except for the following, and very important information. 1- OEM versions do not offer any free Microsoft direct support from Microsoft support personnel 2- OEM licenses are tied to the very first computer you install and activate it on. You cannot reuse your license code to reinstall on a new machine, and since you don't get free support, to attepmt to get Microsoft to release your license will cost you a support fee. 3- OEM versions will not allow you upgrade your motherboard, which could be a draw back. 4- OEM versions cannot be used to upgrade from an older version on Windows. Basically, the retail version will give you the ability to continue using the OS and license when you upgrade to a new machine, or hardware."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002DHLVII', 'answerTime': 'Mar 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393920000, 'question': 'This is the NON-OEM version?', 'answer': 'Yes. Also known as the Full version. 32-bit and 64-bit CDs are included.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002DHLVII', 'answerTime': 'Feb 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392105600, 'question': 'what program do i need to print envelopes, letters? this was on my old computer under microsoft works', 'answer': 'Microsoft Works is an abbreviated version of Microsoft Office. Therefore Works will save you some money. Microsoft Office is the gold standard and can be pricey. If you are a student, you may be able to purchase Microsoft Office through your school at a deep discount. Alternately, the trend is toward cloud-based subscription services that you subscribe to; not unlike your virus protection software. Windows 7 is an operating system that must first be in-place before you attempt to use word processing, spreadsheet software, databases etc. Think of it as your software foundation.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002DHLVII', 'answerTime': 'Dec 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386835200, 'question': "I'm needing to upgrade several computers at a local library ... would this work for that? How many computers can this be loaded onto? Thank you.", 'answer': 'You have only a single seat license. You can install in multiple machines but have 30 days to purchase the additional online seat, unless uninstalled from previous machine. Home version was available for three seats.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002DHLVII', 'answerTime': 'Oct 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382598000, 'question': 'Will this work for my Mac computer using bootcamp', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes. See this article for FAQ's and such for installing Windows 7 on Bootcamp--&gt; http://support.apple.com/kb/ht3986"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002EADP1A', 'answerTime': 'Feb 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392278400, 'question': 'I recently received this product in the mail. After the 45min installation was complete the software will not allow me to register. Whats the fix?', 'answer': "I had the exact same problem when I purchased the product by mail through Amazon! I sent the manufacturer an email directly stating the problem and my frustrations. They sent me a product code with a link to download an updated version of the product. It worked just fine after that. However, it was somewhat difficult to navigate through the settings on their website to do it. As long as you can provide something that shows you purchased the product, the manufacturer will provide you assistance. (If you purchased it through Amazon, it will be on record anyway.) It's a pretty good product overall though as a supplemental learning tool for Spanish! Best wishes! -Charlie"}
