{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002JYU5WI', 'answerTime': 'Mar 29, 2011', 'unixTime': 1301382000, 'question': 'Win 7 Home 64-bit to Professional 32-bit: When upgrading from Windows 7 Home Premium 64-Bit to Windows 7 Professional, will it give me the option to install the 32-Bit version (perhaps even a dual-boot)?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'No, you\'ll need to use the CAD program in XP Mode. The "Anytime Upgrade" doesn\'t "install" anything. It activates features that are inactive until the key is entered. If you have 64 bit, it stays 64 bit.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002JYU5WI', 'answerTime': 'Apr 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397026800, 'question': 'Are we sent the download code via e-mail, or do we need to wait for something to come in the mail?', 'answer': 'We can email the code or if you order on Amazon you will get a factory sealed product with the code inside.'}
