{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002JYU5WI', 'answerTime': 'Mar 29, 2011', 'unixTime': 1301382000, 'question': 'Vista Home Premium to Win7 Pro: If I buy this "anytime upgrade" thing, will I be able to do what I want?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Vista requires an upgrade license and DVD. "Anytime Upgrade" is for those who already have Windows 7 Home Premium. Vista Home Premium and Windows 7 Home Premium are not the same product.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002JYU5WI', 'answerTime': 'Dec 1, 2011', 'unixTime': 1322726400, 'question': 'How much extra does it cost for the download link after one purchases the dowload code? Is it too much to ask to send the download link with the code.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Ever watch "The Wizard of Oz"? You had it with you all along, every copy of Windows 7 (and Vista) has all the bits and pieces for every edition. (from memory) hit the Windows (aka Start) button, type \'Windows Anytime Upgrade\', and it should load up the interface to enter the code that unlocks the pro features.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002JYU5WI', 'answerTime': 'Dec 17, 2010', 'unixTime': 1292572800, 'question': 'Upgrade from Windows 7 Home Premium to Windows 7 Professional in SPANISH: Anybody knows this ?', 'answer': 'Win 7 Ultimate can handle 35 different languages, not sure if Spanish is among them, but I suspect it is, and the tendency is to make it possible to switch between versions with just a language kit.'}
