{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002PRIT0O', 'answerTime': 'Oct 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414738800, 'question': 'Can I save the story files to the cloud rather than to the folder with the application?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "You'll want to save it to both. I am saving my story to its folder within the software, and to a flash drive, Carbonite backs up my computer daily, and I save it also to Google Drive so I can easily import my changes to my PC from my laptop. Tip: whenever you close the software it saves the story, so if I open it from the cloud, I always do a save as and save it back to my Writeitnow folder so that I am working within the computer. This is important because then you can Ctrl S and save as you go. When you're done you can save it to the cloud again. Hope that makes sense. Good luck!"}
