{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002SR4S0Q', 'answerTime': 'Feb 2, 2010', 'unixTime': 1265097600, 'question': 'Charitable Contributions: Does H&amp;R have a list of common household items and their approximate donated value?', 'answer': 'For the past few years, Taxcut has come with an extra disk called Deduction Pro. That program helps you calculate your deductions and includes the fair market value for common items. I think it is included with the deluxe and premium editions of H&R.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002SR4S0Q', 'answerTime': 'Dec 19, 2009', 'unixTime': 1261209600, 'question': 'Saving TaxCut Tax File: Has this changed?', 'answer': 'Yes it does, as of 2007. Go to menu "file", and then save as PDF will come up. It will prompt you to download PDF995 freeware, which I did, then you can both save and send as PDF file.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002SR4S0Q', 'answerTime': 'Dec 29, 2009', 'unixTime': 1262073600, 'question': 'State Tax eFile: My question to TaxCut is will the 2009 version support the eFiling of the Arizona state return?', 'answer': 'TaxCut does offer state e-files, but you need to buy the correct version of the software, which costs a little more with state e-filing. Check the package material and then go to the "update" section, hunt around in the offered state updates until you find the correct one WITH e-filing. Also be aware that states get updated when they can be, not all at once, so AZ might not be available yet, when others are. Patience is a virtue. Dave S.'}
