{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002UEKTK0', 'answerTime': 'Nov 30, 2012', 'unixTime': 1354262400, 'question': 'can my husband and i use this program on two different computers ,his and mine seperately', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, Fluenz authorizes three activations on three separate computers. If you are using the same computer with two different accounts/logins, the program will ask for a authorization number for each account but only one activation will be used because the Fluenz system recognizes the one computer ID.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002UEKTK0', 'answerTime': 'Jul 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406185200, 'question': 'What is the difference between the Spain and Latin American version?', 'answer': 'The largest superficial difference is that Spanish Spanish pronounces the soft "c" sound (pronounced "see") like "th". For example "conoce" (you know) is pronounced "konosay" by Mexicans and "konothay" by Spanish. However the deep difference is the structure of the language. You could say the Mexican Spanish is "street" Spanish whilst Spanish Spanish is "classroom" spanish. If you speak Spanish Spanish where I live in Texas the Mexicans will laugh at you, sort of like, "hey, listen to the professor!". If you\'re going to Spain then learn Spanish Spanish but if you want to talk to Latinos in the USA speak Mexican Spanish.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002UEKTK0', 'answerTime': '9 days ago', 'question': 'Does the program have a voice response for proper pronunciation on words?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Hi John, There are exercises in which you record yourself and playback to compare to the original. As for voice recognition software, there is not. We don't believe the technology available is at a sophisticated enough level to always give accurate feedback, and when speaking any language there is so much to be considered such as the pitch, the tone, the speed of what is being said, if the speaker has an accent, which syllables or words to stress, etc. We want to avoid telling a user through our course that something is being said correctly or not after being analyzed by the program, when they would likely be understood speaking on the street. Cheers, Fluenz"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002UEKTK0', 'answerTime': 'Dec 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418544000, 'question': 'Does this set come with a download option? My mac does not have a DVD drive. I want to get the 123 set first before getting the 1-5', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. I just downloaded 123 today, and It works fine.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002UEKTK0', 'answerTime': 'Jul 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405062000, 'question': 'is this a good product for homeschool foreign language or more directed towards adults?', 'answer': 'Hi! Thanks for you interest in Fluenz. We have several homeschool students that use our program. We typically recommend our program for ages 12 and up. However, we have many kids younger than this that use our program. The main factor in determining if it is a good fit for your child is their level of reading comprehension. If your child can do the demo, they will have no problem doing the program. You can view our free Spanish demo here: http://fluenz.com/languages/learn-latin-american-spanish/ If we can help further, please email us at: usersupport@fluenz.com Cheers, Fluenz User Support'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002UEKTK0', 'answerTime': 'Jul 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404198000, 'question': 'Can this be played on a dvd player instead of a computer?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No, this is an interactive program. Computer only.'}
