{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0036Z0NZI', 'answerTime': 'Jun 4, 2010', 'unixTime': 1275634800, 'question': 'Is the license of the Microsoft Office Home and Business (disk) perpetual? If a computer crashes or is replaced by another computer can the license of the crashed/replaced computer be used on a new replacement computer?', 'answer': "Yes, it can. I've replaced my laptop and desktop once since I got O2007 and the only thing I had to do is call an 800# and an automated system activated it for me without any hassle. It's pretty painless. I'd assume O2010 works the same way. Also had replaced a machine since Win7 was installed and it was the same painless process."}
