{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0039L2XG6', 'answerTime': 'Feb 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391414400, 'question': 'Microsoft Excel Upgrade from 2003 to 2010: If I buy Microsoft Excel 2010 to upgrade from my current Excel 2003 will I have problems with it erasing other data in my computer when I install it?', 'answer': 'Installing a new version of Excel will not erase your current excel files. Version 2010 will open version 2003 files & after you edit them with version 2010, you will be prompted to save them in the newer Excel format. Version 2003 saves your Excel files as "name.xls," version 2010 will save them in the newer format, "name.xlxs." You shouldn\'t have problems with backwards compatibility between file extensions. After you install the new version, make sure you update it immediately. Micro-Soft does have an extensive Knowledge Base at their Excel home page. (Your paying a lot for this software, utilize them!)'}
