{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003FW4O16', 'answerTime': 'Aug 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407999600, 'question': 'I am having trouble finding an exact match of OS X 10.5 for my 2005 iMac PowerPC G5 which is currently running OS X10.4.11.', 'answer': "Michael I believe you're looking for Tiger and thats kind of hard to find... well hard to find cheap. They are out there however upwards of $100 that I could find. The trouble your going to run into is that the system itself will run ok however when you start using the internet thats when your system slows way down because the newer internet systems require newer pluggins that are not backwards compatible and will cause your older OS to lockup a lot!! And in a lot of cases you will not be able to access your e-mail so the sad news is that it might be time to consider looking for something late 2012 or newer."}
