{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003XKRZES', 'answerTime': 'Jun 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370934000, 'question': 'I recently discovered that my imac does not have idvd installed-only iphoto and garage band. Is this dvd an original installation or an upgrade only?', 'answer': "The Original&,everything up to present!(Really can't go Wrong!!).I have no regrets!. I hope this helps:)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003XKRZES', 'answerTime': 'Feb 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1360483200, 'question': "is iDVD '09 is better then iDVD '11 version?", 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "I own iLife'04 and iLife'11 but not iLife'09. The promos and packaging of iLife'11 suggest the major improvements since iLife'09 are to iPhoto (v.9), iMovie (v.9), and GarageBand (v.6). Although iWeb and iDVD are are again included in the 5-app iLife'11 bundle, I don't think there's been much if any change to these apps since iLife'09. The version of iDVD that came with iLife'11 was v7.1 (so you can check against your current version). Personally, I needed iWeb v3 to solve v2 backwards compatibility problems."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003XKRZES', 'answerTime': 'Oct 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381993200, 'question': 'Can I upload only the iDVD program? My iMovie 11 does not have iDVD. If so, is there anything else I should do to make the iMovie &amp; the iDVD programs compatible?', 'answer': 'Yes you can. But make sure you have a backup through Time Machine. The upload of iDVD may mess up iPhoto.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003XKRZES', 'answerTime': 'Feb 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1359964800, 'question': 'Does this version come with iDVD and iMovie?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes it does. I only chose to install iDVD as the newer Macs don't come with it. I kept the current version of iMovie and it works fine with the older version of iDVD."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003XKRZES', 'answerTime': 'Feb 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1360051200, 'question': 'what version of iPhoto is on this disk?', 'answer': "9.0 is on the disc. Once you install it from the disk, you'll want to immediately update it BEFORE launching iPhoto for the first time. There is a data loss bug in 9.0. The latest version is 9.4.2. Enjoy"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003XKRZES', 'answerTime': 'Nov 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383724800, 'question': "Can this be installed separately without writing over the existing iLife '09? I'm not as interested in iPhoto, but more for iDVD and iMovie.", 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "I don't know about not writing over iLife '09. However, when I installed the old version of iLife 11, the installation DID NOT write over my iLife 6. So your guess is as good as mine!!!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003XKRZES', 'answerTime': 'Jul 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374908400, 'question': 'Does it work with OS X Snow Leopard 10.6.3', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I do know about Snow Leopard, it works with the latest ver of mountain lion'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003XKRZES', 'answerTime': 'Mar 21, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426921200, 'question': 'Will this work with OX S Yosemite, 10.10.2?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "As was explained to me at Apple, the iLife '11 is necessary to install OSX Yosemite, 10.10.2. Hence it precedes Yosemite. Therefore, if your Mac has Yosemite, then the iLife '11 features are already available. At the same time, if you do not have Yosemite then iLife '11 is a necessary software upgrade to install Yosemite properly. I hope this helps."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003XKRZES', 'answerTime': 'Mar 1, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425196800, 'question': "Will this work with Mavericks 10.9.5? I would be buying it for iMovie '11.", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I have Mavericks 10.9.1, and I bought it for iMovie '11. It works great - assume that it would for 10.9.5 as well."}
