{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003YUJBXK', 'answerTime': 'Dec 24, 2012', 'unixTime': 1356336000, 'question': 'Hi I wanted to know if this program is used for Spanish- Dragon Dictare, or which I recommend to dictate in Spanish.thanks', 'answer': 'Hi; At this time Dragon Dictate does not make dictation software in Spanish. In January 2013 look for possible upgrades then. The only thing available at present would be windows dictation scratch Pad, this program does process Spanish-language among others.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003YV62CM', 'answerTime': 'Sep 28, 2010', 'unixTime': 1285657200, 'question': "I think I'll wait on this one. Why did I buy all this ram if nothing uses it.... ??!!", 'answer': "David, Premiere Elements comes with a Help application that launches when you select the menu Help&gt;Elements Organizer Help, or Help&gt;Premiere Elements Help. This way, we can refresh the content frequently and address common questions. Alternatively you will see a link to the URL in the top right corner of the Help application, which you can bookmark. A 3rd option is that you click on the View Help pdf file, also in the top right corner of the Help application window, if you wish to save it to your harddisk or print it. Please note however, that the pdf file won't be updated during the course of the product release, whereas the online Help resources will. If you are still stuck and need further assistance, please contact Technical Support at 1-800-833-6687, Monday-Friday, 5am-7pm PST. Regards, Adobe Tech Support"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003YV62CM', 'answerTime': 'Jan 9, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420790400, 'question': "I know Windows 8 isn't listed, but does anyone know if it works on it?", 'answer': 'Yes, it will'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003YV62CM', 'answerTime': 'Jan 28, 2011', 'unixTime': 1296201600, 'question': 'Changing Format: And, can I use my mts files and burn them to a standard, non-HD, DVD?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It's not really a converter but you can output to mpeg, avi, adobe flash video, windows media, quick time, and also to the ipod etc... And yes you definitely can burn your HD mts files to standard DVD. But if you want to do a lot of HD editing you will need a powerful computer, above the minimum requirements set by adobe."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003YV62CM', 'answerTime': 'Sep 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379228400, 'question': 'Is this program compatible with windows 8? If not, what are my options?', 'answer': "I'm sure the horrible experience I had with buying Adobe Premiere Elements through Amazon isn't typical, but it was a nightmare, and I would never risk trying to buy it again. Through some unfortunate snafu, I was sold an OEM version of the program which isn't supposed to be sold on its own like regular retail software. It wouldn't work properly, Adobe support tried to help but said the problem stemmed from the fact that it was an illegal copy. Long story short--My brand new computer was scrambled, I had to wipe its memory clean and start over, and Amazon issued me a refund. My strong recommendation is that you buy Power Director from Cyberlink. It costs less than this Adobe program, is fast, easy to use."}
