{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0043T6LHA', 'answerTime': 'Dec 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418716800, 'question': 'DOES 2010 ALSO DO 2009?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'Nope. Tax law is, unfortunately, very fluid and changes from year to year. The risk is that you would end up not taking advantage of deductions available or, worse, taking advantage of deductions that have expired and having the IRS audit you.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0043T6LHA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 5, 2011', 'unixTime': 1299312000, 'question': 'Turbo Tax Deluxe (Federal + e-file + State) - filing 2 state returns: Does anyone know whether TT Deluxe (federal + e-file + state) allows you to file 2 state returns without an additional charge provided I am NOT e-filing my state returns?', 'answer': 'I have never tried to do this myself, but it is my understanding that you would not be hit with an additional charge. (I am assuming of course that this is two returns for the same state. You only get one state included. If you need to file a return for more than one state, you would be hit for $39.95 per additional state).'}
