{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0045WAF9U', 'answerTime': 'Jun 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371711600, 'question': 'I use Quicken 2007 and Quicken Essentials. Does CheckBuilderPro interface with these?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "You'd just be double inputting data. I use Quicken for all my finances and CBP for writing checks. It's easier and less convoluted. I write the check and just input the transaction in quicken."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0045WAF9U', 'answerTime': 'Feb 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1361779200, 'question': "I'm on a MAC. In addition to CheckBuilder Pro software, what other software, if any, is needed and recommended. And what brand check blanks? THX", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'You can use check paper from suppliers like VersaCheck or many others. I use "stub-check-stub" business format and get my checks from ASAP Checks, Forms and Supplies ( asapchecks.com) product number BSBM-2500 which is 2500 checks in a box. No other software is necessary, except that we use CBP to only print blank checks and use our accounting software to actually fill in the checks.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0045WAF9U', 'answerTime': 'Sep 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378710000, 'question': 'Where is the register?', 'answer': 'Once you have selected the Checking account when the program opens, the check register can be selected from the "file" menu. It allows you to track your checks similar to how you would with a manual register. I only use the program to print blank checks that are then filled in with other software. The remainder of the instructions are on pages 20-22 of the CBP manual which is found under Help and is in pdf format.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0045WAF9U', 'answerTime': 'Jan 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420185600, 'question': "Must you use MICR toner? Sounds like people are using their regular printers so I'm confused.", 'answer': 'I use a regular epson printer, or HP laser....'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0045WAF9U', 'answerTime': 'Jan 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390809600, 'question': 'Use Quicken 2007. Lost input back to 3/15/13.Made new register starting Jan 1st. Have 250 Intuit checks. Will CBP help from Intuit. Will CBP help me?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "CBP will keep a running register for you (if desired), or you can just use the program to design and then print blank checks (for use in Quicken). It's a 2 or 3-step process to make all this happen. 1) I design and print checks in CBP on my laser printer (about 100, using blank check stock; 2) I run these checks thru my color printer to add my business logo (Skip, if you don't need this); 3) then I use QuickBooks for Mac to print the actual completed check. Hope this helps."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0045WAF9U', 'answerTime': 'Jan 7, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420617600, 'question': 'I have an ink-jet printer, can I use the laser personal check stock or is there a special personal check stock for ink-jets?', 'answer': 'I use the check stock in my Canon ink-jet and the checks work just fine at the bank.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0045WAF9U', 'answerTime': 'Jan 7, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420617600, 'question': 'I want to put a background picture on my personal checks, does anyone sell canvas-style check stock for this or can I just use white?', 'answer': 'Hi. I use Versacheck personal checks or also have used Checks-Personal Pack check blanks. I import an image from my computer and use that as the background image. Hope that this helps you.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0045WAF9U', 'answerTime': 'Nov 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415260800, 'question': 'What kind of printer is needed? Any?', 'answer': 'The software is for printing checks -either filling in payee, amount etc. on preprinted checks, printing blank checks to be used in other software such as Quick Books, or for doing both at the same time. Likewise with deposits. The software can also manage your check register and deposit register. I use it for printing blank checks and deposits to be used by other software. Having said all that, therefore a printer is needed. It will print to most printers I believe. As for the way we use it, we print via a laser printer with a MICR cartridge to make sure the check account line is encoded the way banks require it to be encoded magnetically.'}
