{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0048NUNY8', 'answerTime': 'Jan 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390809600, 'question': 'I saw that the QB POS 2013 was good for Windows 8 on another site. But this does not indicate it will work with a Windows 8 Platform. Will it work?i', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes! QuickBooks Point of Sale works great with Windows 8. When you purchase from Ability Business, we can offer you great support to help get you up and running.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00493WILI', 'answerTime': 'Dec 14, 2010', 'unixTime': 1292313600, 'question': "How does this compare with Master Cook 11? Can you import Master Cook 9's recipes? How does this compare with Master Cook 11?", 'answer': "Hi, Yes, Living Cookbook can import MasterCook recipes from all versions of MasterCook. There is an FAQ article that explains how it works: http://www.livingcookbook.com/support/faq/article.aspx?id=31 Living Cookbook 2011 is compatible with Windows 7 (and 98, 2000, Me, XP and Vista). There is also a page on LivingCookbook.com that compares Living Cookbook 2011's features against MasterCook 11: http://www.livingcookbook.com/product/compare.aspx Please let me know if you have any other questions. Lee Grainger Living Cookbook Developer"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00493WILI', 'answerTime': 'Aug 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377327600, 'question': 'Will this product work with Windows 8?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. I have it working on my laptop which has Window 8.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00493WILI', 'answerTime': 'Aug 8, 2011', 'unixTime': 1312786800, 'question': 'mac version: I now have a Mac and was wondering if there is a Mac or web version?', 'answer': "Hi, No, we don't have a Mac version of Living Cookbook but there has been enough interest that we are considering developing one. Lee Grainger Living Cookbook Developer"}
