{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004I45BLW', 'answerTime': 'Jul 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374649200, 'question': 'If multiple recipes on your shopping list have the same ingredients are they listed next to each other so you can easily consolidate amounts?', 'answer': "Wish I could help but I don't use the shopping list function Judy"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004I45BLW', 'answerTime': 'Jul 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374217200, 'question': "Can you save weekly plans so that you might have 4 'standard' weeks that you could just rotate through?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'You can save weekly menu plans in the "Notes" section and you can retrieve the plans as desired. You can have shopping lists for multiple recipes to simplify shopping.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004I45BLW', 'answerTime': 'Apr 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1366786800, 'question': 'can you scan recipes in to macgourmet if you have a scanner?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes! You can scan a recipe to a text file and drag the file to the clipping option of MacGourmet. I've done it many times with no difficulty. I also the copy the recipe image and paste it in."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004I45BLW', 'answerTime': 'Sep 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379833200, 'question': 'Can you import from mastercook? I need to switch, as mastercook has no Mac program.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Importing Recipe ML, MasterCook MXP & MX2 and Meal-Master files To import a file: Using MacGourmet, choose File &gt; Import... Choose the file you want to import and choose the appropriate file format, RecipeML, MasterCook MXP & MX2 or Meal-Master. This is copied from MacGoumet Deluxe's help. I like it."}
