{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004Q0PSMK', 'answerTime': 'Nov 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385107200, 'question': 'If I have a problem and have to reinstall this Win7, can I re-install? Someone mentioned that it is a one time only install. Is that true?', 'answer': "Technically yes. However, the License is good for one PC and one installation, however you can perform an inplace repair installation (by using the upgrade option) by launching the setup program via the installation media from within Windows 7, and if you need to completely reinstall the operating system (where you might re-format the Hard Drive) despite it being activated a phone call to Microsoft's Activation hotline may allow you to use the key again as long as it's on the same computer. They're usually pretty helpful if something goes wrong with your 1st attempt at installing their software."}
