{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004Q0T0LU', 'answerTime': 'Aug 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377154800, 'question': 'Can it be installed on multiple computers', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No, this is an OEM (original equipment manufacturer) and single use disc for installation on new build. I would also recommend new motherboard and memory if you decide to buy. With 64bit you are not limited to 3GB memory maximum on 32bit systems. I purchased this item because I was dumping all my 32bit windows XP Professional systems and building new 64bit systems with multiple cores and maximum memory. You can reinstall on same computer up to 3 times after that you may have problems activating. Also after install if you change too much of your hardware it will affect your activation. http://www.microsoft.com/licensing/about-licensing/windows7.aspx'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004Q0T0LU', 'answerTime': 'May 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1368687600, 'question': 'does windows 7 professional come with word, powerpoint, and excel?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No it does not, you have to order Microsoft Office.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004Q0T0LU', 'answerTime': 'Jul 31, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375254000, 'question': 'Can you use this 64-bit Windows 7 to overwrite Windows 8', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I bought a HP desktop and use this to over-write with it, it didn't work for me(won't format). It required me to have Win 8 OEM to unlock some sort of setting in F8. HP don't included the disk so i did another way... I just bought a Samsung SSD for it. If your situation is like mine, maybe you can do it my way : ) Change from Disk drive to SSD is much faster."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004Q0T0LU', 'answerTime': 'May 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1368342000, 'question': 'Can I use this product to downgrade from Windows 8?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes 100% yes, I personally did it. However be prepared youtube has may videos on how and why just be prepared to mess with the drivers for your computer and the bios. Also tech support with almost disown you -source personal experience'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004Q0T0LU', 'answerTime': 'May 26, 2011', 'unixTime': 1306393200, 'question': "Will this work in Apple's Boot Camp? Are there any issues with using OEM versions with the current version of Boot Camp?", 'answer': 'I just installed it with bootcamp on my iMac. No big problems. Needed to use a wired mouse during the install. Also it had me format the bootcamp partition before the install, very quick (just followed the prompts). After the install on the windows side. The magic mouse didn\'t seem like it was going to work, but took several seconds then it did. There was no sound and the resolution looked terrible. Needed to install the drivers for the sound card and video card... these are on the Mac OS disk (just pop it in and run it on the Windows side and follow the prompts). Everything is running smooth and looking good. I installed a few windows programs (which was what I had wanted Windows for (a few programs I run that don\'t have mac versions)). This is a fresh install so no problems that I can see at this point. No significant install troubles. My iMac now automatically boots Windows, press and hold the "alt/option" key during power up and you can select either Windows or Mac OS to use.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004Q0T0LU', 'answerTime': 'Dec 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387353600, 'question': 'is this disc for a fresh brand new install or is it only an upgrade? I am looking to to wipe my computer and will need a fresh install.', 'answer': 'Fresh new install.'}
