{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004QMT9D2', 'answerTime': 'Jan 22, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421913600, 'question': "Can I convert regular CD's to mp3 files with this?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Actually on Windows, I convert my CD\'s to mp3 using the included Microsoft Media Player. Under the "rip music" tab in the preference you can select the format as "mp3" and dial up the "Audio Quality" to as much as 320 bps. Once set in preferences it runs automatically every time I stick in a CD. You don\'t need to add software to do this. For me the sound quality seem great ... but do note I am no longer a young person and my hearing is not what it used to be ... so this particular part of my opinion should be taken with that in mind.'}
