{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0051M6I9O', 'answerTime': 'Sep 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378278000, 'question': 'Will this software play Blu-ray discs? If so how well laid out is the movie player (if there is one)?', 'answer': "This software use Apple Quicktime, and Windows Media Player 9, to play the movie clips you have made and preview your compilation. I don't know much about Apple software, but Media player versions 7 and above all play BlueRay discs, so you should be able to preview BluDisc clips and rendered files. I don't know if you can use Veags studio as a media player program, as it will only play the video in the preview panel. Probably will not give you access to the menu and settings part of your disc. Of course you must have a BluRay DVD drive on your computer."}
