{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0051M6IPI', 'answerTime': 'Mar 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425283200, 'question': "I've been using Windows Live Movie Maker to edit video, but am tired of dealing with that program's numerous glitches. Is this a good upgrade?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I'm glad I made the move to Sony Vegas. Not that I didn't enjoy Movie Maker, but Vegas gives me so much more control. Also, I can see things on TV or in a movie and think about it a minute, then realize I can make the same effect happen with Vegas. It just takes some practice. Also, you'll want to acquire Bill Myers' 101 Tips and Tricks DVD. It will give you a great idea of just how much you can accomplish on Vegas and how easy it is, once you learn the tricks."}
