{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005FIWTHO', 'answerTime': 'Nov 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416729600, 'question': 'can quicken 2012 be used on windows xp?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes, but I am curious why you are interested in an older version of the program? DO NOT GET QUICKEN 2014 as its functionality is less than earlier versions. 12 may actually have been my fav. Attaching documents to my transactions is my issue. In earlier versions I could attach Checks or Invoices or Other. When I wanted to view an attachment I chose one of the 3 categories and picked my image. In 2014 there no longer seperate categories. You have to selec, then open, each individual image to find the one you need.'}
