{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005FNVINU', 'answerTime': 'Dec 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386489600, 'question': 'making labels from address book', 'answer': "Sorry I never used the Hallmark Card Maker, to any extent anyway. It was not very user friendly. One thing I did not like was you could not delete the Hallmark information/logos. When I make a card I don't want people knowing I was using a stencil. I had been using a card maker program that is no longer available and it was easy to use."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005FNVINU', 'answerTime': 'Aug 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376204400, 'question': 'Will it work on Windowa 8 CP ?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'As my computers use either Windows 7, Vista or XP, unfortunately I have no knowledge of Windows 8. However, a quick Google search suggests that some people are having a problem using their Hallmark software in Windows 8 but several are reporting that when they disable their Norton Anti-virus program and/or their firewall, it works fine. You could try doing that. Sorry that I cannot help you further.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005FNVINU', 'answerTime': 'Jun 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370847600, 'question': 'how do i change my email address on my email a card', 'answer': 'Hi Chrissy I am not exactly sure what you mean. Do you mean that you have more than one way of emailing, for instance Hot Mail or Yahoo and you wish to change it from the default email address? I only have one Virgin Media email account so when I click on "email" within the Hallmark program, it automatically takes me into a new message in Windows Live Mail (my operating system is Windows 7) so I put in my recipient\'s address and then send it on its way via my Virgin Media email provider. On the other hand, when it first goes through into your default email, instead of "sending" it, you could "save" it to "My Documents" and then go into whichever email account you wish to send it from and add it as an attachment from "My Documents". I have just tried saving it and you can then attach it to any email. I hope this information helps. Angela'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005FV8RV8', 'answerTime': 'Jun 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371106800, 'question': 'This is an Academic version.If I buy by Amazon how can i be sure it will run?Do I need send certifications to the manufacturer after receivin the box?', 'answer': "In order for your Sibelius to run you must submit proof that you are a student/teacher. The easiest way to do it (I did it) is using your school's email address, ie. tiara_still_fly@yourschool.edu. They want to see an edu ending. They will send you your activation key through that email. You can also fax/email your school ID card and they will send you the activation key the same way you sent your ID."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005FV8RV8', 'answerTime': 'May 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399273200, 'question': 'How many licenses does it come with? Could I purchase this software and have two students on two different computers use it simultaneously?', 'answer': 'I believe it can only be used by one workstation at a time but Avid would need to confirm that'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005FV8RV8', 'answerTime': 'Oct 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380783600, 'question': 'Is it easier to transpose music on sibelius 7?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yup, there is a button in the top menu. It also asks if you want to use double sharps or flats.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005FV8S4O', 'answerTime': 'Nov 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384588800, 'question': 'Does anyone know what the difference is between Sibelius 7 Academic Student edition,and the Academic Teacher edition? They have different part numbers', 'answer': 'Thank you for your question. The software itself is exactly the same, and sells for the same or close to the same price. The only difference is that the student edition includes 4 years of free upgrades. AVID is fairly strict about verification, so you definitely need to provide verification that you are a student or teacher to qualify for either of these two academic editions. I hope this information is helpful. - Arnie Schachere, Music Studio Direct Amazon Store'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005FV8S4O', 'answerTime': 'Nov 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384588800, 'question': 'Is this identical to the Sibelius 7 Academic product offered on the Avid website for $295, including all packaging and documentation? thanks!', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes it is the full box product, but you have to have an educational email account in order to use this. There is no key in the box, but once you authenticate yourself as a student or teacher they send you a product key in the mail.'}
