{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005MMMT6E', 'answerTime': 'Oct 12, 2011', 'unixTime': 1318402800, 'question': 'Adobe Photoshop Elements 10 vs MacbookPro 10.7 Lion? Can this software be used on the new MacbookPro 10.7 (Lion)?', 'answer': "I have PSE 10 running on Lion. The only thing I can't seem to do is get my raw files (pics) to load directly from the organizer into the raw software instead directly into the editor. Therefor, I can't edit in raw. This copy of PSE 10 was downloaded from Adobe."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005MMMT6E', 'answerTime': 'Jul 6, 2012', 'unixTime': 1341558000, 'question': 'Download vs. mailed to me', 'answer': 'Easier reinstalls when a machine replacement (planned or unplanned) is needed. My most recent case was unplanned after a machine crashed, but previous years it was planned.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005MMMT6E', 'answerTime': 'Dec 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419840000, 'question': 'My laptop is dying. Can I use this version (10) that I already own on a second (new) laptop that I have just ordered, or will I have to repurchase?', 'answer': 'You should be able to use it on the new laptop. Do you have a hard copy of your version 10 and the License Code? If so, then just install it from your disk and enter the License Code when asked. If not, you can clone from one laptop to the other (e.g. using Casper), but I would likely check with Adobe support on the best way to accomplish your needs if you installed from a download.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005MMMT6E', 'answerTime': 'Jan 12, 2012', 'unixTime': 1326355200, 'question': 'RAW Format: Can I edit RAW images with my new Nikon D300S with Elements 10?', 'answer': 'For the D300S you need Camera Raw v5.5 or above. PSE 8 shipped with 5.5, so PSE versions 8 and above should handle your NEF raws.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005MMMT6E', 'answerTime': 'Aug 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408258800, 'question': "Is it better than the elements 7 I'm using now. In the version I'm using, lettering appears to be overlaid by a mesh. Will upgrading cure this?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I have never used version 7 so am not aware of exactly what the issue is. I have not had any issues with the appearance of lettering in Elements 10. Besides, the newer features of v9, v10, etc. make upgrading worthwhile, I suggest.'}
