{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005N2CSLY', 'answerTime': 'Dec 9, 2012', 'unixTime': 1355040000, 'question': 'Can you copy a tree to CD with images?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'You can create a "book" which would take some effort but it does allow you to add images. The book can then be saved as a pdf. You can export trees as Family Treemaker files with images/media, but the user would have to have FTM to open them. GEDCOM files, a universal file system, do not support images.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005N2CSLY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395817200, 'question': 'Can you transfer your whole Ancestry.com tree (and/or specific entries) into a Family Tree Maker program, or only the reverse?', 'answer': 'Yes, you can transfer all of your ancestry.com research onto the Family Tree Maker - pictures, notes and all.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005N2CSLY', 'answerTime': 'Sep 14, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379142000, 'question': 'Does anyone know the difference between this version and the newest 2014 version that just came out?', 'answer': 'Not much of a difference - you can still pretty much do the same things with both (books and all) and can still sync to ancestry.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005N2CSLY', 'answerTime': 'Apr 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1366959600, 'question': 'Will Family Tree Maker Platinum 2013 work with Windows 7?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I have Windows 7 and it's working fine for me."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005N2CSLY', 'answerTime': 'Oct 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382166000, 'question': 'Are you having problems with the display? Mine is too large in places, teeny in others.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Don\'t exactly understand what you mean by the word "display". If you mean the grid with all the relatives and generations past, you sometimes have to drag it up or over to make everything seen.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005N2CSLY', 'answerTime': 'Jul 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374303600, 'question': 'Comparison of FTM Deluxe and Platinum?', 'answer': 'The additional cost is offset by 6 months of free membership which is also good as a credit toward your current active subscription/. It includes a good FTM manual that would cost extra. There is an additional CD to give to a friend but that would require full membership dues.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005N2CSLY', 'answerTime': 'Jan 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1357891200, 'question': 'I have some very old files/pre 2007/FBC.FTW. Will I be able to load this onto this software and see all my info such as pics Ive saved and such?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'As long as your files are not from the original Family Tree maker you should be alright. The only thing is is that you can not go back to the older version of FTM unless you make a copy. Also it is recommended that you use the backup file if you have lots of pictures and documents because a GED does not save them but will reference them as a source.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005N2CSLY', 'answerTime': 'Sep 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378710000, 'question': 'How do you access the ancestry.com membership that is supposed to be included in this?', 'answer': 'If you were luck and received all 3 cd\'s then just go to help inside family tree maker and click on "Activate Ancestry Subscription"'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005N2CSLY', 'answerTime': 'Jan 21, 2012', 'unixTime': 1327132800, 'question': 'Can the free 6 months be added to a current paid account? Will the free 6 months be added to my current account?', 'answer': 'it says that you can on Ancestry.com'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005N2CSLY', 'answerTime': 'Feb 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1361174400, 'question': 'Does the gift disc work on a Mac computer?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'No, the gift disc is formatted for a pc. However, it would probably work if you have Parallels installed on the Mac.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005N2CS8M', 'answerTime': 'Feb 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1361692800, 'question': 'I have Family Tree Maker by broderbund, version 8. I need to upgrade. Can I upgrade to FTM 2012 by Nova?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "You shouldn't have any problem. I have used FTM for years and generally upgrade about every two versions. It is generally seamless. I am using FTM12 now and had no problem upgrading."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005N2CS8M', 'answerTime': 'Jan 21, 2013', 'unixTime': 1358755200, 'question': 'Is Family Tree Maker Deluxe 2012 the same as Family Tree Maker 2012 Complete?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The Nova Development manufactures and sells Family Tree Maker Deluxe 2012 and they have 3 related products. Essentials, Deluxe, and Platinum. They do not have a Complete so I'm not sure what that is. The difference in the three products has nothing to do with the FTM 2012 itself, it is the same in all three. The differences lie in the extras that are included. For example with Essentials you get a 1 month free membership to Ancestry.com, with Deluxe it is 3 mo and with Platinum it is 6 mo. There are other extras as well. I realize this doesn't really answer your question, but I hope it helps."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005N2CS8M', 'answerTime': 'Jan 7, 2012', 'unixTime': 1325923200, 'question': 'Another ancestry.com question... Is it possible to extend a current subscription to ancestry.com with the "free trial" included?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. It took a week or so to show up on my account page, but my last purchase of FTW included 30 days free and it was added on to the length of my current subscription.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005N2CS8M', 'answerTime': 'Dec 28, 2012', 'unixTime': 1356681600, 'question': 'Is Family Tree Maker Deluxe 2012 compatible with Windows 8?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, it is. I was leery about buying it with my Windows 8 computer but it works just fine.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005N2CS8M', 'answerTime': 'Jul 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374562800, 'question': 'I cannot open my older version of Family Tree Maker, if I buy will I be able to open it on windows 8?', 'answer': 'hello Pat, I purchased Family Tree Maker Deluxe and I love it. It is compatible with WindowsXP which I use and also with Vista and Windows 7 and 8 . I hope this helps in your decision. Good Luck, Pat Burdick'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005N2CS8M', 'answerTime': 'Jan 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388822400, 'question': 'What does Family Tree Maker Deluxe [Old Version] mean? Is there a new version which has some significant difference from the old version? If so, what is that difference?', 'answer': 'the Old version has no tie ins with ancestry.com.IOt also ahs a better entry page than the"newer\' Versions(which tie in with ancestry.com and is now up to version 2014. The site ancestry.com contains numerous wrong items. They claim you will see a leaf and it brings up information on the highlighted person. I tried the newer version and the "leaf" information had no relation to the person . Example: I could be looking for George Washington (The first president) of Virginia and it gives me a George Washington Married to "Sue Smith" . We all know President Washington was married to Martha. Many consumer watchdog sites say thee same thing.The site ancestry.com amy shoe relevant info but insist you subscribe to actually see the info. Recently they had a free trial and I did try the free access and all people I searched brought no correct information.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005N2CS8M', 'answerTime': 'Jun 21, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371798000, 'question': 'If I pull pictures, etc from Ancestry.com to Family Tree Maker and later cancel ancestry.com, will my pictures still be viewable or only the links?', 'answer': 'Your pictures should still be there in Family Tree Maker even if you cancel Ancestry. To make sure, I would download them to a flash drive or somewhere else on your computer and that way you would have them for sure. I always put my Family Tree Maker onto a flash drive and that way if something happens with my computer I have all of my information still in tact. It is always good to have a back up on Family Tree Maker for all of the work that we put into it. I teach Researching Family History and use Family Tree Maker and always tell my classes to back up your information.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005N2CS8M', 'answerTime': 'Jan 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1358064000, 'question': 'I am currently using Family Tree Maker 8.0 by Banner Blue. Which version should I buy which will allow me to upgrade my existing data base?', 'answer': 'I never heard of the program you have but family tree maker 2012 gives you acess to ancestry.com and it allows you to search their data base for info you may not have. I truely like this program. I hope this was helpful.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005N2CS8M', 'answerTime': 'Apr 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1367046000, 'question': 'Will this work with Mac?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'There is a mac version, looks like amazon has it for $99.99'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005N2CS8M', 'answerTime': 'Oct 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382511600, 'question': 'I have data on FTN v 2011. can I import that data directly to FTM v 2012', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Follow these steps. First back up your FTN data. Next open FTM v 2012 and select import. Search for the FTN data which could be Hack.ftn (the name of the family tree or similar.) Ignore the screen about back up first since you already backed up your FTN data.'}
