{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006CVV4HE', 'answerTime': 'Aug 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375513200, 'question': "What product should my 21yo use to refresh her Spanish? Hasn't taken it in 2 yrs and has to take college level 2 class to meet a requirement. ugh.", 'answer': "I have used Rosetta Stone (pricey), duolingo.com & udemy.com. I think udemy is the best but there's no oral component and it starts off very slow for someone who already knows the basics. If you already speak well, then you could probably skip some and do fine. Duolingo is completely free, but I had trouble with the speaking part. If you don't need this, and are just looking for a review, this would probably be your best bet."}
