{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0073LIDE4', 'answerTime': 'Oct 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383116400, 'question': 'Is this a trial or year?', 'answer': "It's the full-version, the serial number is tied to your amazon account."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0073LIDE4', 'answerTime': 'Oct 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380870000, 'question': 'why doesi it say it is only a 30 day trial?', 'answer': "You have to provide the serial number to unlock. Click on start trial, then it will tell you there's a newer version. Download, install and run the new version. Then enter the serial number (which should show under the product name in your software library on Amazon."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0073LIDE4', 'answerTime': 'Oct 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380783600, 'question': 'Serial number does not work. I copied and pasted it exactly. Error message says the number does not match the product version.', 'answer': 'Okay, after a bit of frustration, I got mine to work (same problem). I clicked on the "start the 30 day trial". After doing that, it pops up a box that says I have an outdated version and an option to click on a link to get the updated version through Corel. I clicked on that, chose my operating system and downloaded the update. After install, the same box pops up to register the product and it worked.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0073LIDE4', 'answerTime': 'Oct 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380610800, 'question': "Where's the license name when register? I can't find it in the email. I can find the serial number, but not license name.", 'answer': 'If you\'re talking about the dialog form box that pops up when you install Aftershot Pro, when it asks for "License Name", it\'s asking for your name. You can enter whatever you want there. The "Serial Number" box must match the serial number you got in the email.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0073LIDE4', 'answerTime': 'Sep 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378364400, 'question': 'Does thes "PC download" include the linux version? Also, what version/release of AfterShot Pro is this download?', 'answer': "I don't think it includes the Linux version. I bought this about 2 months ago, and the PC version downloaded from Amazon was slightly older than the latest one that's now available on Corel's website. Latest version is 1.2.0.7, and it's available for download directly from Corel (http://www.corel.com/corel/pages/index.jsp?pgid=800161&ppid=4300004). I purchased through Amazon but did not install Amazon's version. I got the license key from Amazon, then downloaded the latest version directly from Corel (the latest version 1.2.0.7 is a full installer package), installed it and entered my license key to activate the latest version. I'd be surprised if you couldn't do the same with the Linux RPM or DEB installer."}
