{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007BG9VLK', 'answerTime': 'Jun 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370847600, 'question': 'vista', 'answer': 'Vista? If you are referring to MS Vista, Lightroom 4 will run on Vista with Service Pack 2 according to the information on the box.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007BG9VLK', 'answerTime': 'Jan 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1359360000, 'question': 'before I purchase lightroom 4, will it work with vista service pack 2,intel core 2 duo 32 bit. thankyou. David.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Lightroom 4 supports Vista 32bit - Although I highly recommend running Win 7 64bit. http://www.adobe.com/products/photoshop-lightroom/tech-specs.html http://helpx.adobe.com/lightroom/kb/optimize-performance-lightroom.html Lightroom is cross-platform and includes installers for both Mac and Win, so there isn't a specific version/license for Mac and Win."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007BG9VLK', 'answerTime': 'Mar 27, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427439600, 'question': 'Will Lightroom 4 work on a pc with Windows Vista SP2,Intel Core 2 Duo T8100 - 2.10 GHz-4 gigs of RAM- NVIDIA GeForce 8400M GT with 256 MB memory?Thx', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, it should run just fine. I am running it on a PC with a dual core approximately 2 GHz AMD processor , Windows VISTA SP2, 4 gigs of RAM and a much less powerful video board than yours.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007BG9VLK', 'answerTime': 'Apr 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1366959600, 'question': 'How do I maintain keyword list as I set it up?', 'answer': 'You can use the keyword panel in the Library module to maintain and organize your keywords. More on Keywords from the Lightroom Manual: http://help.adobe.com/en_US/lightroom/using/WS25DB0AC8-EEDE-4246-B3FE-D20D128B5EB4.html'}
