{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007HCU8QK', 'answerTime': 'Aug 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376895600, 'question': 'is it easy to use', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'It is reasonably easy to use, however the manual leaves a lot to be desired and needs a lot of work. You have to figure out a lot of things yourself but once determined it is easy to use!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007HCU8QK', 'answerTime': 'Jul 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373266800, 'question': 'a. how does this work, with a computer? does it downgrade the quality?', 'answer': 'I have been using it with a Windows 7 machine and so far have found no degradation in the quality of the video transferred and copied to a CD. I have transferred 8 VHS tapes so far with great resolution!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007HNWJIO', 'answerTime': 'Sep 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379055600, 'question': 'Can you print checks from this software?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No, check printing is not possible-nor desirable, really-for this simple but essential piece of software. It very capably does what no other app can do: let you know when bills are due, how much money you\'ll need for upcoming expenses, and a history of what was paid and when. This is not a bookkeeping program like "Quicken," but it does exactly what it says it does, and does it well.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007HNWJIO', 'answerTime': 'Oct 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382598000, 'question': 'can you transfer quicken files and keep a check book with this item', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "No, this is not a money management tool in that sense. But it does one thing well, better than Quicken or any other app: records who you owe, when it's due, and when and how much was paid, with alerts and reminders and such as needed. Frankly that's the only thing that was missing in my money management arsenal. Nothing else gives me-quickly, with no fuss-a snapshot of exactly how much needs to be paid out. A great app."}
