{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007IWCWFE', 'answerTime': 'May 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1368428400, 'question': "What versions of Corel are available for upgrade - i have an old version that doesn't work with my Win 7 upgrade", 'answer': 'You can upgrade from x4 or x5 but not including academic versions'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007IWCWFE', 'answerTime': 'Mar 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1362816000, 'question': 'Will the upgrade work with windows 8?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I only had CD6 for about a week (and never opened it) - I had tried to use the demo one with Win7 and didn't like it so I sent the package back (I don't remember now what I didn't like but I use CorelDraw X5 with my business and Windows 7 on all my computers and have not had the desire to switch to Win8 (it just looks more like a toy than something I need for production) and I keep all my computers with the same OS if at all possible. So, in answer to your question, I'm really not the one to ask on either question. Hope you find out."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007IWCXHG', 'answerTime': 'Feb 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392278400, 'question': 'The latest OS you are listing is Windows 7. However, on the Corel website X6 Graphics Suite X6 is listed as Windows 8 compatible. Please advise.', 'answer': 'It is Windows 8 compatible. The Corel website confirms it.'}
