{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0081TYO6I', 'answerTime': 'Dec 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418025600, 'question': 'I recently purchased this item and find it wonderful! I would like to know how to enter my merchant number maunualy so i can run credit cards.', 'answer': 'In the POS software, the Merchant Service provider should be (connected or embedded with in the POS software itself once you have chosen which Merchant Service you use. This is done within the POS software and Merchant Services once it is set up). I too had this issue with the basic card swipe with this package. I installed an Ingenico IPP 350 PIN pad so that all is run thru the PIN pad "NOTE"(be sure to find a PIN pad that works with your Merchant Services. In many cases you can not install a generic, it has to work with your Merchant Service provider). This also gives you the ability to accept debit cards so the customer can input their PIN Number. I hope that this makes sense, if not just contact your Merchant Service Provider and they can assist you in setting this up thru your POS Terminal.'}
