{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008MR365O', 'answerTime': 'Sep 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379660400, 'question': "I need to know if my dictation will be 100% in Spanish. i don't need a translator only a system that will be exactly in SPANISH only", 'answer': 'Dragon no es un traductor, sino un transcriptor de voz que escribir lo que le sea dictado. El programa "sabe espaol", de manera que ir escribiendo lo que escucha con la correcta ortografa del espaol. Finalmente, un detalle importante, el programa va a prendiendo ms a medida que es usado, pues incorpora aquellas palabras que no conoca a medida que tiene "ms experiencia" con la propia voz, estilo y vocabulario de cada usuario. En fin: nada que temer.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008MR365O', 'answerTime': 'Apr 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1367046000, 'question': 'Dragon NaturallySpeaking Home 12 Spanishs run with PCI of Windows 7 Home with 64 bits', 'answer': "Hi Graciella. I have Dragon Naturally Speaking Home 12 Spanish installed in a pc with Windows 8 64 bits and it works great. I haven't had any problem using it at all."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008MR365O', 'answerTime': 'Aug 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408690800, 'question': "I understand that Dragon's Spanish version also comes standard in English, that if one wanted to change from one language is that the case?", 'answer': 'With DNS Spanish version you can dictate in English. You just need to produce a separate profile for the English dictation. From what Nuance told me, the English versin does not work in Spanish. If you need just English, you can get it way cheaper that the Spanish version. But, if you need to dictate both in Spanish and English, like I need, then the Spanish version is the only one.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008MR365O', 'answerTime': 'Jul 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405753200, 'question': 'i want to know if home Spanish 12 include the head-microphone', 'answer': 'Yes it is included'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008MR365O', 'answerTime': 'May 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400137200, 'question': 'Does this allow me to dictate both in English AND Spanish?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'hi Jorge. no, the Spanish 12 Home, it does NOT allow for English dictation. only Spanish. However the Spanish 12 Premium edition, DOES support both Spanish AND English dictation (user profiles). here on Amazon, i notice the seller named "DragonMaster" has the Spanish 12 Premium edition for a right good price, with very fast service and good ratings. Check it out.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008MR365O', 'answerTime': 'May 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399791600, 'question': 'Does it work with Windows 8.1', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'According to the product website it indicates that Dragon Naturally Speaking 12 is compatible with Windows 8 both 32 and 64 bit versions. I have only installed this program in Windows 7 64 bit.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008MR365O', 'answerTime': 'Dec 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387353600, 'question': "Can I use the English version of Dragon home to speak Spanish as well? I don't need the materials/box to be in Spanish.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'That has been my own question to Nuance for several years now. Their answer is a definitive NO, so far. The Spanish version can be used to dictate in English, but the English version does not accept Spanish speech; since it does not have the vocabulary, etc. (I wish Nuance would change their mind, since Nuance sends all of us nice offers for the English upgrades, while we have to pay full price for the Spanish upgrade).'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008MR365O', 'answerTime': 'Dec 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385884800, 'question': "Informed that the Home 12 Spanish version is bilingual (Spanish-English) However, I can't find confirmation of this in description ofproduct.True?", 'answer': 'Its not bilingual. I recommended the same version but blue box, called premiun.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008MR2I8U', 'answerTime': 'Nov 28, 2012', 'unixTime': 1354089600, 'question': "Why would I need to purchase the seperate Kap internet antivirus as well? Shouldn't this cover me for everything? (legit question, not a complaint!)", 'answer': 'Kaspersky\'s "Internet Security" (usually more expensive) is an fancier version of "Anti-Virus" (usually cheaper). You pick one or the other, do not purchase both. This website shows the differences: http://usa.kaspersky.com/renewal/home-user-renewals Oddly, the back of the Anti-Virus box has a more better breakdown of the differences. I don\'t know why they don\'t put that on their website.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008MR2I8U', 'answerTime': 'Nov 28, 2012', 'unixTime': 1354089600, 'question': 'How long of a subscription comes with this anti virus software?', 'answer': 'It comes with 1 year of a subscription. You can put it on 3 computers, but the subscription starts from the day you first put it on the first computer. Make sure to uninstall all other (including Kaspersky) anti-virus software before installing. (Do not use the internet, meanwhile!)'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008MR2I8U', 'answerTime': 'Nov 27, 2012', 'unixTime': 1354003200, 'question': 'How can I know that this "box" comes with a 12 month subscription to updates? It\'s a lot cheaper than other prices, so I\'m a little suspicious.', 'answer': "I have it installed and it updates every day itself if I stay on line for awhile or you can update it your self any time you want. This is the second year I've used this product and it seems to work well."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008MR2I8U', 'answerTime': 'Nov 26, 2012', 'unixTime': 1353916800, 'question': 'is it compatible with windows 8?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'According to Kaspersky\'s website their 2013 Anti-virus is "Windows 8 Compatible". Website: http://usa.kaspersky.com/renewal/home-user-renewals'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008MR2I8U', 'answerTime': 'Oct 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382252400, 'question': 'Will this work with apple mac desk tops', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Sorry mate this version is for Windows there maybe a MAC version try kaspersky.com'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008MR2I8U', 'answerTime': 'Sep 21, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379746800, 'question': 'Do I have to buy and install 2013 before I can buy &amp; install 2014?', 'answer': 'No'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008MR2I8U', 'answerTime': 'Sep 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378364400, 'question': 'Does this product include an upgrade to KAV 2014 when it comes out?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "You can always upgrade to the next year's version if you have a valid license with time on it from the previous year. After installing the 2013, just download the new version and save it. Then uninstall the old version, making sure that the box about saving the activation code is checked. Finally, install the new version you've downloaded. It should find the activation code automatically. I've done it many times over the years. It's never failed. Be SURE that you match the type of new product with the old for it to work!! For example, if your old version is Anti-virus, be sure you don't replace it with Internet Security if you intend to use the same license. Also, if you have one year, 3 users, be sure to stick with that, too."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008MR2I8U', 'answerTime': 'Aug 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377586800, 'question': 'will it run on older XP machines with 2GBytes of RAM ?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'yes. I am running this on an older netbook witb 1gig ram and a small hard drive.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008MR2I8U', 'answerTime': 'Jun 7, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370588400, 'question': 'for what period of time is this anti virus good?', 'answer': "Clock starts when app is first installed on 1st PC ... subsequent PCs clocks are linked to this first installation date. App will be automatically updated with then current virus databases. Automatic updates expire after 1 year, but app is still functioning; although database will not be updated. That's when you re-order another year ... or as I do, order another 3-PC version."}
