{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008MR2IDK', 'answerTime': 'Apr 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1367132400, 'question': 'can it be installed with the cd on a computer already installed with a soon to expire kaspersky internet security program ?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'if it is already installed on your computer, then there is no need to install again ... only need to enter the activation code which should be printed on a label on the CD ... open Kaspersky program and you will find a label / button saying "Insert your activation code here" on the lower right corner. Even if you want to upgrade to a later version (e.g. you have 2012 and want to install 2013), it is easier to upgrade by downloading from their website (to ensure you have the latest version) than install from the CD as long as your license is still valid (if expired, then enter the activation code first to renew/extend before upgrade). Hope it helps!'}
