{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008NP76AQ', 'answerTime': 'Feb 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391500800, 'question': 'What is the difference between the varios versions of Dragon?', 'answer': 'Paul I do not. I just know that For me the big difference is the ability to use the same profile (the recognition of a certain spoken word which becomes a written word) on multipile machines. Dragon learns as you go if you correct the mistakes it makes. You want to save this learning http://www.nuance.com/ucmprod/groups/dragon/@web-enus/documents/collateral/nc_025214.pdf'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008NP76AQ', 'answerTime': 'Jan 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388822400, 'question': 'Is Professional 12 available for Mac?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No - there is only one version for Mac which is called Dragon Dictate (version 3.)'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008NP76AQ', 'answerTime': 'Mar 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1364108400, 'question': 'i need this professionally for text in german and english - is this in version 12 included??', 'answer': 'There are separate Dragon products for German. There is a Dragon 12 German Premium product and a Dragon 12 German Professional product, each of which might be appropriate. Availability in the US is limited, some certified Dragon dealers such as ourselves would be able to obtain it (expect delays of several weeks) but you may be better off finding a European dealer. The German version includes English. Decide whether you need Premium or Professional based on feature comparisons available for the English editions as these differences are essentially the same in the German editions.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008NP76AQ', 'answerTime': 'Jul 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405321200, 'question': 'does it do excel', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "Dragon works extraordinarily well with Excel. With text entry and with numerical entry Dragon NaturallySpeaking has surpassed 99% accuracy for my use. The one quibble I do have with it is that I've yet be able to successfully remap all the keys from the number pad to other hotkeys in order to not interfere with numerical data entry in Excel. The other small quibble is that auto complete in Microsoft Excel 2010 does not work smoothly with Dragon. This can lead to repetitive data entries which are similar but not quite identical which leads to the need to make manual corrections in your data sets in order for pivot tables and data comparison to work smoothly."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008NP76AQ', 'answerTime': 'Dec 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387094400, 'question': 'Does it work with Android 4.2 and above? Thanks, Steve G.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'This particular version of Dragon Naturally Speaking is designed to install on MS Windows. You can probably use your Android device to record an audio file to upload to your Windows based PC, like a dictation device.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008NP76AQ', 'answerTime': 'Jan 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388822400, 'question': "I'd like to evaluate this software. Is there a return policy if it doesn't meet my needs?", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'I believe Nuance will give you 30 days. Let me show you my demo (I used Medical version though) that I created to show a friend http://www.flickr.com/photos/little_pooky/10578881796/ It works quite well as long as you speak clearly.'}
