{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008RW3XIO', 'answerTime': 'Dec 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385971200, 'question': 'What extra do we get with the MSDN subscription ? Does the VS pro has a in depth help function or that comes with MSDN subscription? Thanks', 'answer': 'The Visual Studio product has an extensive Help utility. However, this is the same documentation that is available publicly online through Microsoft\'s website. The MSDN subscription entitles you to live support (via chat or phone), automatic updates, access to the Team Foundation Server (TFS) portal, a starter account for Windows Azure ("cloud"), e-learning opportunities and more. Using the TFS portal is particularly useful if managing a team of developers (2 or more). If you are a good self-learner, developing for personal use only, or you are a team of one, the benefits of Visual Studio can be realized without the MSDN subscription.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008RW3XIO', 'answerTime': 'Jan 7, 2013', 'unixTime': 1357545600, 'question': 'Does this include MSDN specifically the operating systems portion?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The sub $500 Visual Studio Pro 2012 does not include operating systems or MSDN, just the usual API and tools help files. Pro with MSDN is twice the price. You can download a free trial of Visual Studio Pro from Microsoft's web site."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008RW3XIO', 'answerTime': 'Sep 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378623600, 'question': 'Does it include Visual Basic 2012?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It includes VB.Net.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008RW3XIO', 'answerTime': 'Jan 7, 2013', 'unixTime': 1357545600, 'question': 'c++ is included?', 'answer': 'Visual Studio Pro 2012 does compile native C++ and includes an updated MFC library with many bug fixes.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008RW3XIO', 'answerTime': 'Dec 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386489600, 'question': 'Does VS 2012 require a 64 bit OS?', 'answer': 'No, it will work with 32 bit or 64 bit. VS is a resource hog and will run better with more memory, staying with the 32 bit limits your memory so that alone should make you consider moving to 64 bit for a development machine.'}
