{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008U5EL98', 'answerTime': 'Sep 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380524400, 'question': 'does this support mt2s files?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Hi Dakota, if your camera uses AVCHD (typically stored on an SD card), then the answer is yes. The MT2S file type is primarily associated with 'AVCHD'. AVCHD is a high-definition digital video format that supports 1080i and 720p with a reasonably small file size. AVCHD files are based on the MPEG4 CODEC. AVCHD video files can be burned to Blu-ray discs and played in compatible devices, such as Blu-ray disc players and the Sony PlayStation3. Various video programs can edit or convert this file format which is generally used by Sony and some Panasonic video cameras. I have found that Pinnacle 16 can import almost all video formats currently around. Hope this helps."}
