{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008V4S1GC', 'answerTime': 'Jul 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374994800, 'question': 'does this product automaticly put in ID and password for you', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "No. You don't use an ID and Password to access your McAfee Internet Security software. If you mean does it automatically sign you in to other websites, etc., the answer is also no, which is a good thing. However, the install is VERY easy and once you're a user of it, when you buy a new version next year and install it, it will automatically uninstall any traces of the older version(s). Great product."}
