{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008YTAGIK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 5, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423123200, 'question': 'i need to download this for a windows based virtual classroom will this corrupt any of the data on my hard drive and do i need to install windows', 'answer': 'There is no reason to believe that will corrupt any of your data on the hard drive. Consider it as yet another application you just installed. It is a software layer virtualization engine that will allow you to run windows under your MAC OS and yes, you will need to install Windows as soon as you install Fusion on the hard drive. Hope this helps.'}
