{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0099F823E', 'answerTime': 'Apr 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396508400, 'question': 'Is this price "per seat"? per user? or per machine? or ?', 'answer': "Per machine. Actually, a bit more liberal than that. The Adobe retail license allows you to install it for the same user on two machines provided the two installation are not used concurrently. So if you are an individual you can install it on your desktop computer and laptop computer as long as you don't use them both at the same time, for example."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0099F823E', 'answerTime': 'Nov 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415865600, 'question': 'Can I use this to add password protection to a pdf file?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. You can protect by creating a password required to open the pdf AND/OR to edit or print. There are separate options for certificate security (for groups of people signing and editing common files) as well as file encryption.'}
