{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009B2Z30K', 'answerTime': 'Jun 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372230000, 'question': 'How is it used to teach? And, if so, at what level does it start?', 'answer': 'You first specify which bidding conventions you want to use. In normal play, you bid and play a hand, then the computer bids and plays the same hand and the results are compared. So it is teaching by example.'}
