{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B009SPTUW2', 'answerTime': 'Aug 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408258800, 'question': "Is there a reason that I can't order this for my small business?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I have no idea why you can not get a version of Office 365 Home for your business especially if it\'s in your home. But be thankful for small favors. I used Office 2007 for years and after my year subscription it out, I\'ll go back to Office 2007 much cleaner and easier software to work with, Office 365 is a pain in the rear. you can go on "ebay" and get a copy of Office 2007 Pro or Office 2010 Pro and you\'ll be a much HAPPIER person. With a lot of fewer headaches!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B009SPTUW2', 'answerTime': 'Mar 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394006400, 'question': 'Can I buy this for renewal purpose? i already have office 365, just need to renew. But online renewal is $99. Thanks!', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes! Yes! I did exactly this. Apply the product code to your account. The expiration date of subscription extends by one year.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009SPTUW2', 'answerTime': 'Jul 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406271600, 'question': "Okay, so what's the rub? Word, Excel, PP, Access, Outlook just like at work for $66/year?", 'answer': 'No rub. Having said that, you may be on a different version at work, e.g., Office 2007, 2010, or 2013. However, its compatible, had no problem opening any of the old documents. The catch, you only get 1 terabyte, yes, 1 terabyte of OneDrive cloud storage. So, after you install, just move your documents into OneDrive and you have cloud backup as long as you keep renewing. You can put anything in OneDrive, not just Office files. The software itself resides on your hard drive and updates are automatic.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B009SPTUW2', 'answerTime': 'Mar 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395990000, 'question': "Since I don't own 5 computers or 5 other compatible devices, can i share Office 365 Home premium with other family members?", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, you can go to https://office.microsoft.com/en-us/MyAccount.aspx to invite other users (via email) to share some of your licenses. I don't think you have to log with your own credentials on their machine if you send them an invite that way."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009SPUE72', 'answerTime': 'Apr 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398495600, 'question': 'What is the difference between the PC Download version and the PC Key Card version? Both seem to require you to download the software from office.com. The PC Key Card is cheaper so what am I losing if I choose that option?', 'answer': 'PC Key card version means that they will physically send you a box with a printed key and web site address. You use the key to download the software from that website. This process takes about a week. This means that somebody holds your money for about a week before you get your product. PC download means that you may start downloading right after purchasing the software.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009SPUE72', 'answerTime': 'Apr 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398754800, 'question': 'So if I buy the key card as opposed to the PC download do I have to buy it every year or is it good forever?', 'answer': "The key card is used when the software is preloaded on a new PC. In this case, the software cannot be transferred to another computer and it is good forever on that computer. If you download the software onto your PC, that software cannot be transferred to another computer and is good forever. The only difference is with the key card you don't have to download anything. But in either case the software is good forever on that original computer."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B009SPUE72', 'answerTime': 'Nov 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383897600, 'question': 'If my computer crashes, can I transfer/use this on another computer?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I doubt it. It is registered on one computer. If you were able to use it on another computer, why not 3 other computers. I do know that if you lose Office on your computer you can load it over and over on the same computer. I have done it 3 times due to virus protection wiping out the software.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B009SPUE72', 'answerTime': 'Sep 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411282800, 'question': 'Does this install separately so my older version of Office 2010 will still be available to me? I need to have access to both versions for training.', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "No, it does not. It overwrites the old version. Also the product key does not work if you change your country in installation i.e. you can't buy the product in US and install it in a computer in UK."}
