{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B009YLXNI2', 'answerTime': 'Dec 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387699200, 'question': 'Will this record live steaming content?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The short answer: Yes. The longer explanation: Audials records streaming video such as Netflix, YouTube, etc easily. However it only records video from your TV when used with other apps. Your PC must have a either an attached TV card or video capture device which allows you to view live stream video on your PC, then yes, you can record the streaming video. I, myself, use an AverTV USB HD DVR Capture Device (Model C874) and its associated software: AverMedia Total Media Extreme to view live streaming video. I don't like to record the video in their TS format because the file size is very large, so I use Audials to record the streaming video on the PC."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009YLXNI2', 'answerTime': 'Oct 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382684400, 'question': "Can you burn a streaming video onto a DVD that' can be used on a typical DVD Player? If so, does the vid quality degrade?", 'answer': 'I use Audials MovieBox 10 to record from DVDs and streaming video and then store on my hard drive to watch on my PLEX server. I can say that the videos I have recorded, from what ever source (streaming video or DVDs), had no noticeable video degradation.'}
