{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A9Y478I', 'answerTime': 'Feb 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1361520000, 'question': 'no p.c. in kitchen. can info be easily xfered to an android device like an Acer 500 running 4.03 op.sys.?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I use My Cookbook Pro app from the android play store. You export your cookbook file and save it to your device SD card. I have a Nexus 7 tablet and an HTC One X phone and run the app on both devices. Its not perfect in that they have not added an easy way to sort the recipes from living cookbook but you do have your complete cookbook and just have to go down the alphabetized list to find what you were looking for, They are working on updating the app to work more efficiently with the living cookbook export. they also have easy to follow instructions on their website.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A9Y478I', 'answerTime': 'Jul 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374217200, 'question': 'For meal planning, can you calculate how many times a recipe can be made from your existing pantry inventory?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I honestly haven't gotten around to really plugging in stuff from my pantry inventory yet. This is what the product info says-- Working with inventory: Manage your kitchen inventory. Control the ordering properties of any inventory item (minimum order quantity, order at level, order up to level, etc.). Share inventory data with other Living Cookbook users. Customize inventory displays using your choice of fonts, background colors, headings and more. Create a printable inventory worksheet to help you take stock of your kitchen. Compare any two inventory items side-by-side."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A9Y478I', 'answerTime': 'Apr 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397026800, 'question': 'Once in My Cookbook, is it easy to sort? I might want to title a recipe Thanksgiving Turkey Gravy and be able to find it using any of the 3 words.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, there is a search box called look. You can use look using one or all words in recipe, ingredient, menus, meals, technique, and more. You can also list or sort recipes by Name, Source, and Difficulty.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A9Y478I', 'answerTime': 'Feb 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392105600, 'question': "Can you input your own notes into a recipe? Such as parts of the recipes that worked well/didn't, any substitutions made, etc?", 'answer': 'Yes There is a tip and comment area'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A9Y478I', 'answerTime': 'Jan 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390204800, 'question': 'How many computers can I install this on? I do not see that listed here, should I assume that it is unlimited?', 'answer': '"Please note that Living Cookbook licenses are per-computer. In other words your license can only be registered on one computer at a time". If you need to move it to a new computer than you have to unregister the one you have it on and re-register your new computer. Go to Facts page for more info. I just copied that off of the website that creates this software. Just a extra note; This is the best recipe software I have used. I love it its easy to use and its a great price for what you get..'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00ABAW2UA', 'answerTime': 'Nov 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416643200, 'question': 'Does the license allow the installation of a single copy on 3 computers (same user)?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No. http://www.earmaster.com/support/frequently-asked-questions.html?view=faq&catid= says: Q. I have a 1-PC/Mac license. On how many computers may I install EarMaster? A. The 1 PC/Mac license entitles you to install EarMaster on both a desktop computer and a laptop.'}
