{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AY00DA8', 'answerTime': 'Jul 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374044400, 'question': 'what is different between the 3 version of portrait pro 11?', 'answer': 'The plugin version of Portrait Professional runs within Photoshop so you can retouch an image while you\'re doing other kinds of editing. For a seamless workflow, this is the best option. There is also a standalone version, which runs as a separate software program. It works just as well as the plugin, but you have to open your image in Portrait Professional and then export it. I\'ve used both methods and strongly recommend the plugin. By "three versions" maybe you mean the one that can handle raw files; I haven\'t tried it, but as long as it can work as a plugin it would be worth a try.'}
