{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B1TEIRU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391414400, 'question': 'Can you edit a doc offline? And re-edit it on a different pc with reg office? Created at home and edit at school is the possible situation?', 'answer': "I have Office 365 on two PCs and Office 2011 on a Mac and can work on each the same as any other. I didn't download the Mac version from the 365 suite so I'd say that you could do so. All three are always connected to wi-fi but I don't see why editing a file offline wouldn't work."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B1TEIRU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 5, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423123200, 'question': 'What\'s the difference between "Download" and the "Key Card" since there\'s no disc with either one?', 'answer': 'There is no difference.'}
