{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B1WH7RU', 'answerTime': 'Nov 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383462000, 'question': 'what are the RAM requirements for this program?', 'answer': 'Hi Vickie D, You must have atleast 1GB RAM (if you save in High Definition: 2GB RAM)'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00B1WH7RU', 'answerTime': 'Jul 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375081200, 'question': 'Can you use this program to download videos from youtube', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "No, you are not able to download from YouTube with Muvee Reveal X. I use a program called YTD Video Downloader. This program not only allows you to download from YouTube, but to convert the file into whatever format you need, even audio only file types. Once you have the video downloaded from YouTube, you are able to 'add' that file to your Muvee Reveal project."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B1WH7RU', 'answerTime': 'Sep 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379055600, 'question': 'Does it sync easily to music? Can it be transferred in sync to a stick? Is it easy to e-mail? If so, can it be sent to and read by an Apple? Thank you!', 'answer': "Yes, you can sync your music easily. You can also save on a stick like any other file, just change the destination folder to the stick and you're ready to go. Definitely, you can email the muvees, however, sending videos by email is difficult, because video files are so big. Posting videos to public video sharing websites can mean that your video is there for anyone in the world to see. muvee Reveal provides free online private albums with muvee Cloud."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00B1WH7RU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392537600, 'question': 'Is it possible to clean up the audio "noise" that happens on point and shoot cameras when used for video recording?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No, you will have to download a separate program to cut down background noise. Muvee will not allow you to do that within the program.'}
