{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFNCFXG', 'answerTime': 'Mar 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1364194800, 'question': 'Is x6 32-bit or 64-bit ?', 'answer': 'Hi Bruce, VideoStudio Pro X6 is compatible with 64-bit PCs, but is a native 32-bit application. The happy news here is that VideoStudio offers very impressive support for multithreading, meaning it can take maximum advantage of your multicore processor--delivering excellent speed and performance. I hope that answers your questions!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFNCFXG', 'answerTime': 'Nov 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383552000, 'question': '"Does it do freeze frame? NOT screenshot but the ability to freeze a frame during editing and retain the frozen frame as a clip in the timeline? NOT a capture that exports or saves to somewhere else, but a real freeze frame that stays in the project?', 'answer': "Yes - but not the way you want it to - you just clip a bit of a clip off an existing clip - pretty much a single frame clip of .01 second in length. And that's what you are looking for, I think. If you add a photo to your video, it's added as a 3 second clip - all the same frame. And you have to clip it down anyway, to get just one frame."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BFNCFXG', 'answerTime': 'Jul 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374303600, 'question': 'In my movie, will I be able to show speeded-up segments, like played at 2X speed?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes! While I have not used that feature, the package clearly says "New! Variable speed controls---speed up or slow down any part of your video."'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFNCFXG', 'answerTime': 'Feb 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393401600, 'question': 'I plan to purchase the downloaded version. When I upgrade And get a new computer in the future, will I be able to transfer This software to my new computer? Or Would it be better to order the cd ROM?', 'answer': 'If you purchase a download it will appear in your account so you can download it again.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFNCFXG', 'answerTime': 'Mar 12, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426143600, 'question': 'What is the best video studio to get with no problems', 'answer': 'I gave up on it. Despite my powerhouse machine that edits HD and 2k with no issues, this software crashed.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFNCFXG', 'answerTime': 'Feb 28, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425110400, 'question': 'how many times can i put this on a pc?', 'answer': 'You should only install on one PC if I remember correct. But I think you mean how many times can you download in case you need to get it again. If I remember correct there was a number of times. But when you download the file you will have the file. So burn to a DVD or put on a USB external drive or something so you will have a hard copy of it. What I also did was upgrade to the new version X7. When I upgraded one of the things they offer for a small fee is to mail you a DVD with the program. I paid for it. I feel much better having it here on a DVD. Hope the answer helps.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFNCFXG', 'answerTime': 'Apr 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397631600, 'question': 'This software will create blu-ray discs but will it play them?', 'answer': "I don't know about Blu-ray but the DVD played perfectly."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFNCFXG', 'answerTime': 'Jan 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390377600, 'question': 'How do you get it to recognize a camcorder. Mine works with Skype and MovieMaker, but in X6 the capture for both camcorder and DV are greyed out.', 'answer': 'It has to be a compatible capture device. The key question is what is considered compatible? That I do not know as they refuse to release a compatibility list :( I have ran against the same issue with 1/2 my devices.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFNCFXG', 'answerTime': 'Jan 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390291200, 'question': 'I have Corel Video studio pro x4 and have made a lot of videos with it, however my preview playback is always lagging and jumpy. how does x6 compare?', 'answer': "I also have the pro 4x, I have never had the issue you seem to have. other than the 20 overlay tracks and the 3rd party add on's with the ultimate I can't see any difference. the main reason I upgraded was for these features as well as the price. I got it on sale at amazon and used rewards points on my credit card so it only cost me about $15. When I do a project I always seem to have alot of stills as well as video, for that reason I make several 3 or 4 minute clips saving them in mp4 format, then I stitch them together. That way if I'm well into the project & decide I want to make a change near the start It's no big deal, just change the one clip. Dave"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFNCFXG', 'answerTime': 'Dec 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386835200, 'question': 'I need to import .ctg files', 'answer': 'The .ctg files are cannon catalog files used by canon cameras. They are not meant to be opened by users, but to be used internally by the camera.'}
