{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BFNCFZ4', 'answerTime': 'Sep 14, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379142000, 'question': 'Will Pro X6 insert audio over video? You know, allow me to narrate a video over pictures, music and natural sound.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The answer is Yes. All you have to do is hook up your mic or insert an audio file into the sound track under the video tracks in the timeline.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFNCFZ4', 'answerTime': 'May 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399359600, 'question': 'Does this software rip video from a DVD and then can the video be edited to length and added to other video and is there phone support', 'answer': "Yes, it can be used to rip video from many sources, including DVD's, but I use it to edit my own video that I have shot. Yes, it is easy to edit length, along with many other aspects, like color, clarity, speed and many other tweaks just like a good photo editor would and you can add other video, music, voice over, and photos with a nice moveable Picture-in-picture adding option. There is phone support available for an additional charge, but even better there are many YouTube tutorials and Corel training videos with print instructions available, all for free. I used these free videos & tutorials, along with Corel's Facebook link where other Corel Video Suite owners are very helpful with hints and tricks to help you create professional video footage. I recently used my software to create a television commercial to advertise an upcoming community charity drive to help support Wounded Warriors, last year our community donated over $70K to Hope For The Warriors."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BFNCFZ4', 'answerTime': 'Dec 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386576000, 'question': 'Can you combine still camera pictures AND camcorder video (AVCHD format) on one playable track?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Absolutely!! You can even have photos over video. I love this software!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BFNCFZ4', 'answerTime': 'Dec 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387094400, 'question': 'Has anyone had problem loading .MOV files? Every time I try program closes back to desktop. Using win 8 in win 7 compat mode dloaded latest V6 patch.', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'Video Studio Pro XP cannot handle .mov files. You can use AVS Video Converter to convert the file to an .mpg format.'}
