{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BJ6VMRE', 'answerTime': 'Aug 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408604400, 'question': 'All I need besides this software is a RCA to USB adaptor, correct?', 'answer': "It is hard to answer this question directly since you are asking if you need something that does not and cannot exist. 'RCA' refers to a type of connector while 'USB' refers to a type of hardware-software interface. What you need is a device that converts audio and video to the USB standard required by VHS to DVD. I use a Honestech VIDBOX and I have always assumed that this was proprietary on the USB-software side although I realize now that I am not sure about this. Anyway, I would not attempt to use this software with anything other than a VIDBOX or some similar device that claims compatibility with the VHS to DVD software."}
