{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CS75KKI', 'answerTime': 'Oct 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413961200, 'question': 'I have multiple printed old photos. Can I use this software to edit them once I scan them into a file?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes, but it is more program than you probably need if you are just doing a few personal photos and will not be scanning to and editing in Tiff formate. Adobe also has their Photoshop Elements which should do quite well for you. Plus I believe you can still buy this one (versus rental method of full Photoshop) for about $150 or less. I bought it packaged with Premiere (video editing) a couple years ago. Have used it as well as an older version of Photoshop to scan and edit old photos. It also opens and edits PSD files'}
