{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CSJFWUY', 'answerTime': 'Jun 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401778800, 'question': "I'm a total beginner - is there a required 'drawing pad' or something to go with this or do you use a mouse?", 'answer': "I haven't spent a lot of time working with this program yet but so far I haven't needed a drawing pad, only a mouse and a keyboard."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CSJFWUY', 'answerTime': 'Dec 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417766400, 'question': 'for use simply with posing reference in drawing, how simple is it to get generic poses set up in this version?', 'answer': "To pose a skeleton the way you want with crude background graphics it'd be under an hour when you first use. To pose dressed woman with a pose and nice rendered background will take hours with a couple references to the manual. Once you get experienced It'll get easier and faster."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CSJFWUY', 'answerTime': 'Apr 21, 2015', 'unixTime': 1429599600, 'question': "Will the Library open on a Windows 8 PC? I tried with a Poser 8 and the Library never opened. I couldn't change the character from male to female.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Hello, as a user of p10 on multiple machines I can tell you there sometimes are issues. On my windows 8.1 machine, my avira antivirus kept the library from opening. Any program or firewall that bocks internet access can cause this issue. Smith micro has an updated patch that helps with many of these issues. Hope this helps.'}
