{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CTTEKJW', 'answerTime': 'Oct 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382425200, 'question': 'I Have Amazon Cloud Player on my PC and would like to have it on my laptop also.', 'answer': "No problem. Just install the cloud player app. That's the whole point of the cloud. You can access your MP3's from anywhere and from just about anything that can access the web."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CTTEKJW', 'answerTime': 'Jun 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403247600, 'question': 'My Kindle Fire HDX is giving me a message that says this app is not available on the device. Why is this happening?', 'answer': "I think it is because you don't need an app on the Kindle to listen to your music. Just go to 'music' and it's all there. Instead download this on your computer to listen to your music from Amazon and other music you've loaded into the Amazon cloud."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CTTEKJW', 'answerTime': 'Jun 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402297200, 'question': 'do i need an internet connection to use amazon cloud player?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "If you are using it to download music or play music you've stored in the cloud you will need an internet connection. If you are simply using it as a media player I believe you can use it without an internet connection. To be honest I've found it to be rather bulky and kind've clumsy so I've only used it to download music and then uninstalled the app"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CTTEKJW', 'answerTime': 'Jan 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389513600, 'question': 'can I download this to my laptop', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, I have it downloaded to my Laptop and my Smart Phone. It works pretty good. The only issue I have with the Cloud Player is Album Art. It doesn't show Album Art for all music, even when the Album Art is available."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CTTEKJW', 'answerTime': 'Dec 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386144000, 'question': 'I do not believe this is free, as song storage charges usually appear ! Is there a limit to amount of songs that can be stored free ?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The non-subscription version of Amazon's cloud player allows for the storage of a maximum 250 tracks. The paid version allows for up to 250,000 tracks to be stored, for 21.99 per annum. I believe you need an Amazon account to use the free version, & it comes as an automatic extra if you purchase & register a Kindle HD tablet. A nice touch is that if the tracks you are uploading are in the Amazon catalogue at a higher bit rate, they upgrade those tracks at no cost to the customer. The music can be accessed on up to 10 devices. I have around 480 GBs of music, and to store that as data on a hosting site (for back-up purposes) would cost as much per month as the cloud player does a year )"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CTTEKJW', 'answerTime': 'Dec 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418630400, 'question': 'can you download this music to the music folder on your PC?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes. Either to Windows media or ITunes. Your choice.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CTTEKJW', 'answerTime': 'Jun 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403766000, 'question': 'How do I transfer my Cloud playlist to a thumb drive so I can play it in the car? Specificity would help as I am a techno idiot. thanks.', 'answer': "First if your playlist is mp3 make sure your car will play them. Second what I did was download my list onto my laptop then transfered them to CD's. it may take sometime depending on how many songs you want to download. Cloud should help you step by step to download and your computer music program should offer step by step help to put them on your thumb drive. Hope this helps if you still need help try to find a local computer place to help."}
