{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CY1O8DS', 'answerTime': 'May 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400914800, 'question': 'I have already downloaded a trial from Adobe. It is LR5 v5.4. Is this the same version? Will the Amazon download re-install and keep what I have already started in the trial version?', 'answer': 'No need to reload. When you buy from amazon you will receive a purchase code or unlock code. When the trial version first opens there dill be an option to input the unlock code. Just enter it and you will be set to go. I did this when I got mine. I had a trial version and bout the license and received the code. I input it and all was well'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CY1O8DS', 'answerTime': 'Feb 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393401600, 'question': 'I plan to purchase the downloaded version. When I upgrade And get a new computer in the future, will I be able to transfer This software to my new pc?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes you can. Just go to your amazon account, software downloads, and place it on the new computer.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CY1O8DS', 'answerTime': 'Jun 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402383600, 'question': 'Can you resize pictures so that you can email them easily?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes, very easily. Resizing photos is not a problem using Lightroom 5. It gives you a wide range of preset formats and image sizes to choose from. Very versatile and easy to use.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CY1O8DS', 'answerTime': 'Jul 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374994800, 'question': 'Is this a full version or an upgrade. I have LR4 but my SSD failed &amp; the replacement did too, so I now have to buy a windows OS &amp; I also have to buy L', 'answer': 'Yes it is a full version.'}
