{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00D3BK1PW', 'answerTime': 'May 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401260400, 'question': 'On a 32-bit Dell XPS 600 with 2 drives in RAID, will Linux install okay? Will it preserve or remove the RAID configuration? Thanks.', 'answer': "The answer is probably yes. It will definitely install on a 32-bit Dell XPS 600. I 've had good luck with installing linux based operating systems directly on Dells without having to reconfigure the boot order as you have to do with non-Dell PC's. In terms of RAID configuration, I have no expertise in this area. It probably will preserve the original set-up but I've never encountered this dilemma myself. If you decide to install please let me know how it goes."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00D3BK1PW', 'answerTime': 'Oct 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412751600, 'question': 'Will Linux boot up when I start--Meaning can I get rid of Windows xp', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. It is a full standalone operating system that will replace xp. Download the newest version at linuxmint dot com and donate to the project if you like it!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00D3BK1PW', 'answerTime': 'Aug 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408258800, 'question': 'What are the system requirements? Will all of my Steam game work?', 'answer': 'Yep! Steam supports linux and works great. So far as system req, if you can run steam games you can run linux. Its much leaner than windows. But download the latest version from linuxmint dot com, and make a donation directly to linuxmint foundation. Dont buy this cd sold on amazon here.'}
