{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E1L1P5I', 'answerTime': 'Mar 18, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426662000, 'question': 'I use Photoshop on my Mac, but just got a Macbook Pro and was going to using Manga studio on it. Can I go back and forth with same piece of art.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "In theory yes. I use Manga Studio, Krita, and GIMP. Between those three, the .psd file conversion has no flaws I've found. The real test is how they handle fonts between the two programs. I have no Photoshop, so I cannot verify if it works or not. Just make sure to save images you want to work on between the programs as .psd and IN THEROY, it should work just fine."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E1L1P5I', 'answerTime': 'Oct 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414047600, 'question': 'Is this program something that a very smart (gifted) 9 year old could learn how to use, or is it just too advanced?', 'answer': "Absolutely. I'm way behind on the tech myself and find it not only easy but fun and fulfilling. I had and still have difficulty with photoshop, which was originally recommended for me. I was creating with this within 10 minutes after installation and had an idea of what I was doing. You can create digital paintings with ease and if you want, you can create a comic from ground up. Text, word balloons, everything. I love it!"}
