{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E6LIUO2', 'answerTime': 'Mar 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395730800, 'question': 'Is it a difficult learning curve?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'The learning curve is no more difficult than using any version of QB. You can also go to Intuit Academy 2013 and download a free pdf of 62 page manual that will provide all the detail of receiving and sending Accountant file and using the additional features designed for accountants to review client entries, sending JE only, etc. Saves a lot of your time and reduces client errors.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E6LIUO2', 'answerTime': 'Jan 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391155200, 'question': 'I would like to get QuickBooks 2014 Accountant with a CD, I do NOT want the download version. How can I make sure I get it with the CD?', 'answer': 'First, make sure you choose the "PC" edition, not "PC Download." Under the "More Buying Choices" box, click on the link that says "38 new" (the number may change). Ability Business has a listing stating "Brand New with license in the box" -- this will be a CD with the license.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E6LIUO2', 'answerTime': 'Jun 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401951600, 'question': 'Is QuickBooks Accountant 2014 the same as QuickBooks Premier Accountant edition 2014 that contains reports for various industries?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'yes. you can toggle to another edition. It contains QB premier (general business),contractor, mfg and wholesale, professional services, retail, non-profit, and QB Pro. It does NOT contain QB enterprise.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E6LIM2W', 'answerTime': 'May 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399964400, 'question': 'Does this non-profit software have the abiblity to do payroll?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I am not using the software for payroll. I think there is an add-on that does payroll. On the intuit site it looks rather expensive ($300+ per year).'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E6LIM2W', 'answerTime': 'Feb 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392451200, 'question': 'Never used an accounting software before, just my excel spreadsheets for our small church finances...is this program worth the money?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes! QuickBooks non-profit is definitively worth the money. My husband is a pastor and we use it for our church accounting. It has been a wonderful program.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E6LIM2W', 'answerTime': 'Jan 1, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420099200, 'question': 'is this program usable for canadian churches?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'there\'s a button that simply says "I don\'t know" but that doesn\'t answer the question. What are Canadian church non-profit laws? I\'m not in Canada so in truth I wouldn\'t be able to answer. Happy New Year, however.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E6LIM2W', 'answerTime': 'Sep 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411369200, 'question': 'Is it on a disc or downloadable from the web?', 'answer': 'I ordered it so I would have the disk. I think you can purchase the download from the web if you do not want to have the disk.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E6LIM2W', 'answerTime': 'Sep 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409814000, 'question': 'I would like to see how the forms /reports look. Can I also move the information from quick books 2011 to the new software? TY Bonnie..Treasurer', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Hi Bonnie, You will be able to migrate your 2011 data to the 2014 version. As for seeing what the forms and reports look like, they will not be significantly different from the 2011 version. Intuit does not have a "trial" of the Premier software, but you could download the QuickBooks Enterprise 2014 Trial, it is important that you do not use your "live" data as once the data is converted to QB Enterprise it will not convert back to Premier. After you download the QB Enterprise Trial, when you install it choose "Non-Profit", that will give you an idea on what the reports and forms will look like in the 2014 version. Peter A+ SalesCentral Customer Relations Manager'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E6LIM2W', 'answerTime': 'Aug 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409036400, 'question': "Does QB Premier Non Profit have the capability of creating 1099's with the click of a button?", 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'QB Premiere for Nonprofits is a marketing version of QB Premiere; essentially no differences except the box and an example company in the setup process. I have not processed 1099s yet but their customer service 800-624-1377 or QB chat feature can answer the process for printing.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E6LIM2W', 'answerTime': 'Aug 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408604400, 'question': 'Are there any differences between QuickBooks Premier Nonprofit 2014 and Quick Books Premier 2014, that includes Nonprofit?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "When we bought QB '14 Premier NFP it included all the other choices that came with premier. My guess is that the contents of the box included all that, and that the box may have been the wrong box. I don 't believe you will find any difference once you set up the version that meets your needs. Hope this is satisfactory!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E6LIM2W', 'answerTime': 'Aug 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407135600, 'question': 'I do accounting for a nonprofit with a budget of about $1 million and track about 35 restricted funds. Can QuickBook Premier Nonprofit handle this?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Absolutely'}
