{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E6LIECA', 'answerTime': 'Jan 19, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421654400, 'question': "I don't need payroll for my business. Do I have to give a credit card number anyway when I register? Also do I need to renew every year ?", 'answer': "Hi Peggy, I would not provide the credit card number if I were you. I believe the desktop version is for you to own. You only renew the Payroll Service annually, if you decide to use it. If you are in doubt, call tech support. They'll answer any questions you may have and walk you through. Good Luck!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E6LIECA', 'answerTime': 'Oct 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414047600, 'question': 'Any reason I should not get the 2015 instead of 2014?', 'answer': "If you need any of the new features they've added for 2015, that would be a reason. http://quickbooks.intuit.com/pro/compare/ Also, since they tend to retire support for a version after 5 years or so, you will most likely be able to get updates from Intuit for a longer period with the new version. That's an issue if you need payroll updates."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E6LIECA', 'answerTime': 'Jul 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406703600, 'question': 'capabilities of emailing', 'answer': "I don't use the emailing capabilities. I'm sure it is good. Quickbooks is a great program. I have used it for almost 20 years. There have been many upgrades but this last upgrade is so different and I don't like it."}
