{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E6LIUXI', 'answerTime': 'Sep 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411110000, 'question': 'If I purchase this today (9/17/2014), will I get a free upgrade to Quickbooks Premier 2015 when it becomes available?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Not that I'm aware of. I purchased QB 2010 when it came out and used it for several years until they discontinued services to it. I have had to pay for all newer versions. They give you free product updates to the software, but not to newer versions. I'm not sure how it works with the online version, but this has been my experience with the desktop versions."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E6LIUXI', 'answerTime': 'Aug 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408950000, 'question': 'I do tax work for a dentist. He has recently started his personal LLC. Would this product be a one time go to for all his bookkeeping/accounting needs', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'It depends. Short answer is yes, but depending on how he has the LLC set up it may be better to go with Quicken. If the LLC is set up to be taxed as a corporation then QuickBooks would be the way to go. However if the LLC is set up to be taxed as a sole proprietor, then it would be better to use Quicken.'}
