{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E7XAM4K', 'answerTime': 'Aug 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408086000, 'question': 'Is this a subscription for one year?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The program is good for as long as you want, although there are yearly updates if you would to purchase them. The program will continue to without purchasing the updates.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E7XAM4K', 'answerTime': 'Aug 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408086000, 'question': 'I am trying to figure out what I am getting with this download if I purchase it. Is it just the manual? Do I then have to pay Intuit a monthly fee?', 'answer': 'There is not a monthly fee. You will receive instructions on how to set up your accounts. There are yearly updates that you may purchase if you like but is not necessary for the program to continue to function.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E7XAM4K', 'answerTime': 'Sep 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410937200, 'question': 'can you run payroll with an additional fee on simple start?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes you can. Inside the "Employees" menu you can "Turn on Payroll". Pricing starts at $39 and there is 20% discount at this moment (Sept. 17, 2014). In my case, I use Intuit Payroll beside and I make a direct import/link into QuickBooks.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E7XAM4K', 'answerTime': 'Sep 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409986800, 'question': 'It is not clear if this is a subscription online service product, if so how many months does the current $49.99 cover? 12months?', 'answer': 'I subscribe at $9.99 a month plus tax'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E7XAM4K', 'answerTime': 'Sep 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409900400, 'question': 'I only use Quick Books to make checks. Will this simple one make checks and keep a registar? Also can I buy the disc instead of the download?', 'answer': 'Probably not because this web based "software" offered for $50 (what I paid this past april) is only a trial version. Do not buy this software if you have any remote.idea of trying Intuit\'s 60 day money back guarantee. Approximately 30 days after purchase, I first had dialog with Amazon customer service. In that I was told I would have to go to Intuit. Since Amazon customer service has always served me well, I took the info and called Intuit. Since that call, I have gone round and.round with them claiming to make the refund process simple. ......I still haven\'t gotten my refund and don\'t expect to because of the hassle Intuit has put me through. This software is just the beginning of what Intuit wants to sell you.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E7XAM4K', 'answerTime': 'Aug 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408086000, 'question': 'Will this work with an iPad Mini?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "this month, QuickBooks doesn't seem to work on any of my techno stuff... partially but not fully operational on anything... HP & ACER laptops (3 years old) - home built destop - nor IPad (never used on it... need much more room to see) so the mini is a choice."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E7XAM4K', 'answerTime': 'Aug 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407222000, 'question': 'Does this work with the Quickbooks Point of Sale system?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I doubt it. Even if it did work, Intuit will CHANGE the way the products work AFTER you buy them.. For instance I use QB Online and they changed the way purchase orders are emailed so now they are ALWAYS sent to the spam folder, quickbooks wanted to remove the right of the users to use their own emails and now they are sent from a spammy intuit email address.. Worst company ever, do not trust them.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E7XAM4K', 'answerTime': 'Jun 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404025200, 'question': 'If I use QuickBooks Simple Start and want to upgrade to purchased software in the future, can I move all my data over?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E7XAM4K', 'answerTime': 'Jun 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402988400, 'question': "I have been using 2008 quickbook simple start and need something more advanced. Is this version a better one than I'm using", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. Go to Intuit.com and take a look at the sample pages. It is far better than the simple start'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E7XAM4K', 'answerTime': 'May 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401087600, 'question': 'Can I use this program to create accounts for both my business and my personal finances?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'If your question is whether you can create two separate "company accounts" (one each for business use and one for personal use) under a single subscription, then unfortunately the answer is no. I ended up just using the online version for my small company, and kept using my older quickbooks version for my personal accounting. But if you want to know if you are able to segregate personal expenses from business expenses within a single company account to be able to easily distinguish which items were for business and which were for personal, then the answer is yes. It is very easy to create new charter of accounts and personalize as many expense accounts as you need. The only problem with this though is when you print P/L statements and do not want personal expenses, the report will include ALL expenses, business and personal. Hope this helped.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EAS14KI', 'answerTime': 'Jun 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401692400, 'question': 'Can you edit commeral?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I\'m not sure that I understand the word "commeral" but the Dazzle capture device only captures video. It is the associated software package that comes with it that provides for the editing of video. If the video already exists in digital form (DVD or computer file) there are other comparable software packages available for editing. The Dazzle DVD recorder is typically used to capture VHS tapes in a digital computer based format. Hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EAS14KI', 'answerTime': 'Dec 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418544000, 'question': 'does this device capture in avi?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes it does Dayna. The video editing software that comes with it has this feature in its recording settings.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EAS14KI', 'answerTime': 'Jan 18, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421568000, 'question': 'I can not capture my video using a Hi8 camcorder hooked to the dazzle. Does anyone have suggestions?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Is the Hi8 camera digital? The Dazzle is an analog-to-digital device and should only work with analog video sources. There are other ways to bring digital video into an editing program. On the other hand, if your Hi8 is analog, is it a matter of your editing software not recognizing the Dazzle?'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EAS14KI', 'answerTime': 'Dec 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419926400, 'question': 'So inorder to transfer vas to DVDs on this device it has to go thru my computer? Is this correct? Tammy', 'answer': 'Yes. The unit plugs into a USB port, and is recognized by the computer as a digital input device. You need video capture and editing software to bring over the video and edit and manipulate it in the computer. The unit comes with software for that: "Pinnacle Studio for Dazzle".'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EAS14KI', 'answerTime': 'Apr 23, 2015', 'unixTime': 1429772400, 'question': 'What version of Pinnacle Studio comes with this?', 'answer': 'a very basic one special to dazzle but it works great lots of effects , transitions , titles and stuff and best of all is upgradeable'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EAS14KI', 'answerTime': 'Mar 3, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425369600, 'question': "Does this save my miniDV in digital format (e.g. mpeg), so I can store on ext drive or cloud? I don't want to burn to DVD or upload to youtube. Thx!", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, it save it in digital format (e.g. mpeg),so you can edit it before you upload to YouTube,Facebook...ects'}
