{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EDSI8HW', 'answerTime': 'Sep 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410937200, 'question': 'Whats the difference between this and the oem', 'answer': 'Microsoft did things different OEM-wise with the product SKUs for 8 and 8.1. The difference is pretty much in the legalese. I\'ll excerpt from this write-up here: http://www.infoworld.com/article/2612160/microsoft-windows/microsoft-kills-oem-system-builder-and-upgrade-editions-of-windows.html The author (Woody Leonhard, of Windows Secrets) will tell you a lot, but the bit that he pulled from Newegg is probably the detail you\'re looking for: "The OEM license allows the OEM to resell the PC. The Personal Use license is for individuals who are building (and supporting) their own PCs. Neither are transferable once on the PC, but the OEM license allows for transferring the entire PC to different users." Hope that helps!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EDSI8HW', 'answerTime': 'Mar 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394092800, 'question': 'Can you use the full version of pro to upgrade a windows 7 machine?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Unfortunately the installation does not give you the option to keep your applications, just your personal data. It does save your old application data in a folder called C:\\Windows.old So if you know how or can Google it; it is possible to get your settings back. For example you can find your outlook.pst file, and bookmarks and put them back after you re-install the applications.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EDSI8HW', 'answerTime': '20 days ago', 'question': 'Does it come with downgrade rights to Windows 7?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes. All Microsoft OS licenses allow you to run previous operating systems. See Microsoft's site for more info: www.microsoft.com/OEM/en/licensing/sblicensing/Pages/downgrade_rights.aspx"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EDSI8HW', 'answerTime': 'Feb 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392624000, 'question': 'Is this 32-bit, 64-bit or is it both on the same disk?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I bought this and it included both discs for 32 and 64 bit operating systems.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EDSI8HW', 'answerTime': 'Aug 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407654000, 'question': 'Can this be installed on 3 systems?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Only if you have three different activation codes'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EDSI8HW', 'answerTime': 'May 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400742000, 'question': 'Is this pack the same version as if purchase from MicrosoftStore? In another word I am trying to find out if this is the latest driver? thx.', 'answer': 'Same. Also realize no Operating System installation media has the latest drivers - otherwise they would have to re-package and re-stock too frequently. You just install the currently available version and upgrade the drivers during the upgrade.'}
