{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EFRMECQ', 'answerTime': 'Aug 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408690800, 'question': 'can i backup my computer on a interal hard disk drive', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Sure. But if you are backing-up your OS, you should be doing that to a second physical internal hard drive.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EFRMECQ', 'answerTime': 'Jun 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403074800, 'question': 'Can you use it for 64 bit processors?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes you can, with "NO" problems!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EFRMECQ', 'answerTime': 'Jun 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403593200, 'question': 'Can it restore to a smaller drive, ex: restore from original 250GB to new 160GB drive?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "Using Acronis True Image 2014 Premium's Universal Restore mode you can restore FILES from a larger drive to a smaller drive provided the files occupy less than the 160GB drive space. However, if you are trying to restore an IMAGE of the 250GB drive to the smaller 160GB drive, this cannot be done."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EFRMECQ', 'answerTime': 'Mar 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393660800, 'question': 'What Is (MB)', 'answer': 'It refers to My Backup, i.e. the backup data set produced by Acronis.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EFRMDW2', 'answerTime': 'Jul 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404802800, 'question': 'Hi, can I back up individual files and folders or I just have to specify the whole disk? I am not interested in backing up the OS.', 'answer': "I usually back up full os, but i'm almost positive you can back up individual files. My only gripe with this software is I already owned an older copy and had to purchase a new copy for windows 7!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EFRMDW2', 'answerTime': 'Sep 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379919600, 'question': 'If my computer dies, can the programs and date be copied to a new computer?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'If you backed up your System and you rare running Premium version, you can restore it to a new computer using Restore Anywhere feature.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EFRMDW2', 'answerTime': 'Apr 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396335600, 'question': 'will this program clone copy from old hdd to brand new hard drive completely windows and all?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, I have done that. I installed the new hard drive in the second drive location in the computer box. Then all you have to do is run the clone process. After that completed I moved the drive C: cable to the new drive and removed the old drive from the box. I recommend saving the old drive in case of a failure in the new drive (it happened to me).'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EFRMDW2', 'answerTime': 'Dec 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419062400, 'question': 'How do you only move Windows 8.1 Pro 64-bit from my HDD to a SSD using Acronis 2104. I want my SSD to be my boot drive and my data to be on my HHD.', 'answer': 'I personally found Actonis to be significantly less than useful. Was a poor purchase decision. As far as migration / upgrade of HDD size or types, I simply used windows back-up to create an image on my 3TB external Seagate HDD and a recovery DVD set. Then I did my drive swap, made sure my PC had the DVD as an alternate boot drive and then booted from the recovery DVDs. Piece of cake, albeit a lengthy process.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EFRMDW2', 'answerTime': 'Jan 18, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421568000, 'question': 'Will this software let me clone my entire Windows 7 HP Pavilion laptop to a 3 TB Toshiba external drive?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I believe so. I have cloned many drives to 500gb, 750gb and 1 terabyte drives using acronis software'}
