{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EOI2TD0', 'answerTime': '29 days ago', 'question': 'Can I create avatars and change images to 300 dpi for publishing?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, you can. You need to know what format your environment wants for an avatar, and of course what size. With dpi/publishing, you need to start with the high dpi if you possibly can. If you're using a scanner, set the scan to your target dpi (300 in this case). You can shrink things easily, but expanding things (including raising the dpi) you have to watch out for resulting blurriness. There are adjustments you can then do, but you're better off starting with the high dpi from the get-go. (This is true for all image software, by the way.)"}
