{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EOQZB32', 'answerTime': 'Sep 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410246000, 'question': 'My Microsoft Movie Maker videos are jumpy and unwatchable. Will Premiere Elements provide a solution? Can I convert them to a "smoother" format?', 'answer': "That depends on why your Movie Maker videos are jumpy and unwatchable. If the source files are not jumpy, Premiere Elements would not make them jumpy due to editing. But if the cause of the jumpiness is due to poor-quality source video or not having enough computer processing power/RAM/HD speed, PE won't change anything."}
