{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EPACNBA', 'answerTime': 'May 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400396400, 'question': 'Hello Amazon Customer: Can you please tell me if I can import all projects that was created with Art Publisher 1.0 in the new Art Publisher Pro 3 Pla', 'answer': "Hi Junie, coming from owning a tech support business for over 13 years I do not know why you can not import your Project Files over to the new version. Very difficult to find any place online that says you can't. I setup a ton of new computers for people and move their personal data files over to their new computers with very few problems. You are only moving project files over from a two generation old product so I do not see any problems there unless Nova Development changed their file format for their projects recently. I did not find any mention or come across Pro Publisher changing to a new file format for their publishing program. So I would highly doubt it here in your situation that you would not have any problems being able to bring your old Publisher Project files & import them into the new Publisher Pro 3.0 program."}
