{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EZQYC8G', 'answerTime': 'Jun 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403679600, 'question': 'How long after purchasing can I wait til I download/install? Would like to wait a few months.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'All Norton products come with a security code that needs to be entered before the product can be used. AS long as you have that code the license is valid for one year after installation. Hope this helps....AMaBargain.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EZQYC8G', 'answerTime': 'Jun 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402902000, 'question': 'I just ordered this Norton Internet Security 2014.If I use 15 August of 2014, will it be there till August 2015 or it starts the day i receive it', 'answer': 'Your days begin to count down starting the day you load it on your computer, not when you purchased it. You have a year from this date, but Norton counts the days backwards for you. Norton reminds you to renew. You do not have to keep track. Amazon.com also reminds you of renewal just before your year is up.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EZQYC8G', 'answerTime': 'Aug 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409036400, 'question': 'What is the difference between Norton Internet Security and Norton 360?', 'answer': "Not 100% sure, but it is a more advanced version. I suggest going on Norton's website where they have a video of what the differences is between the two. I may have even seen the video on Amazon. Their video convinced me to go up from the regular anti-virus to the security for more protection with internet buying and banking. Hope this helps."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EZQYC8G', 'answerTime': 'Aug 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409036400, 'question': "is this as good as the 360? I have had Norton 360 for year bought it here for $19.99. Don't really want to pay $39.94 if I don't need it.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The only difference is 360 backs up some files and has a cleaning program that removes junk files periodically. The internet security has all the important stuff to keep your computer healthy and without viruses etc. I wouldn't use the extra parts of 360 anyway and that is why I always get internet security. Only get 360 if you use the other parts."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EZQYC8G', 'answerTime': 'Sep 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409554800, 'question': "Is this software compatible with Windows XP &amp; will it work in Iowa/compatible worldwide? I bought someone else's software and it didn't work for me.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "If it was registered in someone else's name, it probably will never work if you attempt to register it in your own name. It is however compatible."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EZQYC8G', 'answerTime': 'Sep 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410073200, 'question': 'I want to know if it scans the emails also', 'answer': 'It does not scan your e-mail automatically scan your e-mail but you can select and scan e-mail attachments before opening them.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EZQYBZ0', 'answerTime': 'Mar 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395644400, 'question': 'I already have 2013 version and more that a year before expiration what happens if I buy 2014 version ? am I extended another year ?', 'answer': "A few years ago, I renewd a Norton subscription and it added one year from the date I renewed, not added to the end of the subscription. When I renewed with my 2014 subscription, it extended my subscription by a year, adding it to the end of my current subscription, which is as I would expect. So while I can't say which will occur, my most recent experience is that it added time at the end of my current subscription."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EZQYBZ0', 'answerTime': 'Jan 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391155200, 'question': "All these sounds great!!, but I'm new in this game and I want to know; how long can I keep using this unit before it becomes in effective and have to be replaced with a new version?", 'answer': 'We replace outs once a year. Our month is October. That way we are always up to date.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EZQYBZ0', 'answerTime': 'Mar 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395126000, 'question': 'Do you run norton on your computer or how', 'answer': "Yes, and including the kids, we run Norton on 5 computers. On my main 2 we also run a Malware (MalwareBytes) program for back-up security. Norton has always been reliable, but last year I tried the anti-virus instead of the 360 and my computer got real sick, so I went back to the Internet security after I got cleaned and haven't had any real problems since."}
