{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00F3ZN2W0', 'answerTime': 'Nov 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384675200, 'question': 'Is this a full version for a computer that has no operating system', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Yes, the install offers an upgrade or to do a full (clean) install which is what I did. If you're putting an SSD and hard drive in to your machine, don't connect the hard drive until after the install if you want the OS to be on the SSD. The installer can get confused if you have more than one drive available."}
