{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00F8K9KZS', 'answerTime': 'Feb 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393228800, 'question': 'Can I use a prior year Turbo tax to file 2013 taxes...', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't believe you can. Even if it were possible, I wouldn't advise it. To get around the MAC OSX problem, I used the TurboTax online version. I also understand that you can use the H&R Block software and it will allow you to transfer in your prior year information. Good luck!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00F8K9KZS', 'answerTime': 'Jan 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389859200, 'question': 'is this a cd?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Choose PC/Mac option before adding to your cart if you don't want a download version."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00F8K9KZS', 'answerTime': 'Jan 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389168000, 'question': 'If I buy this for filing 2013 tax, can I use the tool to file 2014 as well? My second question is, can I take print out of tax prep?', 'answer': 'I use the 2013 Turbo Tax as a help for me to work up my tax estimates for the year 2014, as I file and pay quarterly taxes. Turbo Tax is helpful in working up the 2014 estimates. You must however buy a new 2014 Turbo Tax to complete your 2014 taxes, as tax rates change and laws change. I am not sure I understand the print question, but you can print out any forms you desire, including any worksheets, and I usually print out my final return before I E-File.'}
