{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00FB5R6L0', 'answerTime': 'Jan 1, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420099200, 'question': 'Does it simply burn a CD and/or DVD from jpegs?', 'answer': 'A jpeg or jpg file is a data file. It contains data for a picture. If you have a picture on your computer, it can be written to the CD or DVD. You would choose the data file option for CD or DVD then drag the photos into the Disc Content box. Watch the green bar at the bottom to see how much you can fill the CD. A DVD has more room. I have family photos on my computer that I have scanned and put them on a disc and sent them to other family members. I also have photos downloaded from the internet that I use for desktop backgrounds. I can put them on a disc also. BTW. Put your music files on as a data disc and you can fit hundreds of songs on one disc and listen for hours. So, use up a few discs to see what works for you. You can also reuse a disc for your experiments.'}
