{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00FB5R4SA', 'answerTime': 'Sep 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411196400, 'question': 'can i copy copywrited dvds onto hard drive. then later copy them onto a blank dvd to watch on a dvd player/tv (I have permission to copy them)', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes. If they are copy protected. Nero will prevent you from copying them. If they are not (and you have permission) you will be able to copy them. The best way to find out if they are copy protected is to attempt to copy them.'}
