{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00FB5R4L2', 'answerTime': 'Dec 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386748800, 'question': 'what i want to do is to download a movie from my thumbdrive in avi or mkv formats, then use the program to make it into a normal dvd. Can it do that?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Hello, I work for Nero and saw your question about Nero 2014 Platinum. Good news: Nero 2014 Platinum is exactly the product you need for converting your movies from avi, mkv, or other formats and burning them onto a DVD that can be played back in any DVD player. Simply start the application Nero Video, select "DVD" -&gt; "DVD-Video", then add your avi or mkv files to the compilation, enter an empty DVD media to your recorder drive, start the burning process, that\'s it. Thanks and best regards, Eduardo Vento'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00FB5R4L2', 'answerTime': 'Jun 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403938800, 'question': 'why does nero 2014 platnium only find one of my two blu ray recorders? both drives are shown in the file mgr. &amp; in device mgr both working properly', 'answer': 'It does not matter if both devices show up. Nero only recognizes one of the devices. The primary one. IF you try to contact Nero they will charge you tech support, and it is not cheap.'}
