{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00FZ0FETC', 'answerTime': 'Dec 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417852800, 'question': 'i ordered the wrong webroot and it wont load on my windows computer', 'answer': 'Try to get your money back. 9 Out of ten times Whn I have a problem with something I ordered online, after writing the seller. I gave me a partial or full refund or they may offer the right one as an exchange. Good luck.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00FZ0FETC', 'answerTime': 'Jun 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402815600, 'question': 'Will I need to remove the virus program currently installed? (Norton)', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "That would be your best bet. I always remove all of my I.S. & Virus systems when installing a COMPLETE all-in-one product such as Webroot (or, any other all-in-one that you may have previously installed), as it has a built-in anti-virus system. If you don't remove your previous system, you could run into future problems of both systems trying to work...and they could end up working against each other."}
