{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00FZ0E0HE', 'answerTime': 'Apr 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427958000, 'question': "I currently have kaspersky but it doesn't protect my internet searches. Does this replace all my antiviruses or can I use both?", 'answer': "I don't know about Kapersky, but SecureAnywhere runs just fine along side McAfee. McAfee did notice it was there and said something weekly stated about it not being wise (or words to that effect) to run two antivirus programs at the same time. That being said SecureAnywhere found and dealt with trogans and keystroke recorders that McAfee never detected. I work in a school district with old computers running XP and using a flashdrive to transfer yearbook related materials to my home computer is where my difficulties have arisen."}
