{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00G6CLNCK', 'answerTime': 'Jun 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403420400, 'question': 'I have burned a project to a disc, I am unable to play it on "older" DVD players. Is there a way to burn it to a disc to solve this?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Linda: Not sure if this will help or not, but some older players such as the Panasonics require only DVD - disks. If you are using DVD+ disks, they will not work in some older players. Newer players can accept both the + and the - versions. Hope this helps.'}
