{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00GIZ4LMO', 'answerTime': 'Aug 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408258800, 'question': 'Is it possible to write for an orchestra, assign instruments of your choice and play back a symphony, for example? Also what are Garritan instruments?', 'answer': "Yes for all. Garritan instruments is a software used to playback your orchestra but it sounds way better than the default sounds. Download the trial, it doesn't come with the garritan instruments, but you can hear the default sounds (midi). The garritan will sound better than that. * you choose your instruments when you set up your score. * to change an instrument, press ctrl+k (assuming you're using a pc)"}
