{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00H09BO2M', 'answerTime': 'Jun 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402124400, 'question': 'can this be used to go from win xp to win 7?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Actually Yes. First install Windows Easy Transfer for XP and export all your settings to and external drive or network share. After Windows 7 installation run Easy Transfer (already in Win7) and restore your settings. This will transfer all your internet settings, favorites, docs, music, pics, etc., but not any of your old programs. Be sure to have copies of programs that you want to re-install after the of Windows 7.'}
