{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00IVFDZBC', 'answerTime': 'Oct 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412751600, 'question': 'Corel WordPerfect easily converts to Word for non-Corel users. Does the Graphics Suite also convert so that Adobe users can work with my files?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes. CDGS can save files in .ai , .eps, . pdf and .psd formats. However, with all such conversions there is always a chance that some aspects of your file may not be included if identical features do not exist between applications (e.g. Photo-paint does not have layer styles so no layer styles are included in an exported psd file and vice versa when importing and exporting psd files).'}
