{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00JHN1MJO', 'answerTime': 'Jul 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405753200, 'question': "does it include payroll? how much it cost for updating after 1 year expire? does it still work for both payroll and accounting if I don't update?", 'answer': 'Payroll is an additional $250 for up to 50 employees. If you want to e-file quarterly tax forms, add $67.50. If over 50 employees add $450 plus $67.50 if you would like to e-file tax forms. Once you purchase the program, Best Business Strategies or any other Sage Solution provider can order that for you. If you are using payroll, you must stay in the most current program and renew every year. At this time, the renewal is $299 plus payroll cost as indicated above. Shirley Byard, Sage 50 Master Certified Consultant, Best Business Strategies'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00JHN1MJO', 'answerTime': 'Dec 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418716800, 'question': 'download bank data', 'answer': 'I download a .QFX file from my bank. It is then imported into the reconciliation. It does not download items that are not in the system to the accounting software, but is does check off the items that are in the system and it tells you what is missing with a red flag. Answered by Shirley Byard of Best Business Strategies.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00JHN1MJO', 'answerTime': 'Dec 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417507200, 'question': 'hello come with your license? to get the program have a year of support, after this year much it costs? how often have to update the program.', 'answer': 'Hi Michele, The exact answer depends on your situation. Are you doing payroll, using Sage Mobile services or credit card processing? If you are, you must upgrade. If not, you can keep your program on your computer for a long time without upgrades if you purchase a BASIC or TRADITIONAL license. Anything that says AUTO RENEWING must be updated every year or the program will stop. The cost is about the same as the original cost of the program less the initial purchase discounts.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00JHN1MJO', 'answerTime': 'Oct 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414393200, 'question': 'Can this version provide simple financial statements? Income statement and balance sheet?', 'answer': 'Yes, it can do all of the above. The biggest difference between this and Premium is that Pro is for one user only and it does not have "job costing". This answer is provided by Shirley Byard, Best Business Strategies.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00JHN1MJO', 'answerTime': 'Jul 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406271600, 'question': 'Can you do the accounting for only 1 business or more than 1 (I need to keep track of 3) with this software?', 'answer': 'Hi Linda, You can manage the accounts for multiple companies using Sage 50 Pro Accounting 2015. You can setup 3 companies if you wish to. I hope this helps. Best Regards Software onFire LLC'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00JHN1MJO', 'answerTime': 'Dec 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419408000, 'question': 'can I do manual tax tables in this product?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Unfortunately beginning with version 2013 Sage 50 no longer has a "manual payroll module". Of course you can always enter payroll (or anything else) in the "general journal". But the manual payroll module, once you set it up, would do the calculations automatically. Sage 50 took that feature away and worse. If you don\'t pay a yearly maintenance fee then you are no longer able to enter new data (90 days after your fee expires it locks you into "read only mode"). It is perfectly understandable, however, since the accounting software business isn\'t what it used to be (due to free alternatives like "Gnucash" so all of these companies have to change their business models. Sage 50 is excellent excellent software. It\'s just not as inexpensive as it used to be.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00JHN1MJO', 'answerTime': 'Nov 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416124800, 'question': 'I have multiple LLCs with multiple rental properties. How many LLCs can you keep track of without having to buy multiple versions of this software?', 'answer': 'I am a Certified Consultant. There is no limit. The limit is not with companies, but with users. Please note, if you want to own your software, you need to purchase the basic or traditional versions. Anything that says subscription is just that. YOU WILL NEVER OWN THE SOFTWARE. Best Business Strategies only sells Basic on Amazon. If Sage says otherwise, they are just wanting your business and not telling the truth about Best Business Strategies. Please note I cannot speak for other Amazon sellers. At Best Business Strategies, we will never sell you a subscription on Amazon. Shirley Byard, Owner, Best Business Strategies. See our store on Amazon. Questions 304-233-2612.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00JHN1MJO', 'answerTime': 'Feb 7, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423296000, 'question': 'Does it include Fixed Assets?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, it covers all the items in a typical accounting package. If you intend to use the payroll module, please be aware that you have to buy their maintenance package in order to use it, which costs in excess of a $1000.00 yearly.'}
